hon 1.6b1.\n\n     4. CNRI is making Python 1.6b1 available to Licensee on an \"AS IS\" basis. CNRI MAKES NO REPRESENTATIONS OR WARRANTIES, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED. BY WAY OF EXAMPLE, BUT NOT LIMITATION, CNRI MAKES NO AND DISCLAIMS ANY REPRESENTATION OR WARRANTY OF MERCHANTABILITY OR FITNESS FOR ANY PARTICULAR PURPOSE OR THAT THE USE OF PYTHON 1.6b1 WILL NOT INFRINGE ANY THIRD PARTY RIGHTS.\n\n     5. CNRI SHALL NOT BE LIABLE TO LICENSEE OR ANY OTHER USERS OF THE SOFTWARE FOR ANY INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES OR LOSS AS A RESULT OF USING, MODIFYING OR DISTRIBUTING PYTHON 1.6b1, OR ANY DERIVATIVE THEREOF, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY THEREOF.\n\n     6. This License Agreement will automatically terminate upon a material breach of its terms and conditions.\n\n     7. This License Agreement shall be governed by and interpreted in all respects by the law of the State of Virginia, excluding conflict of law provisions. Nothing in this License Agreement shall be deemed to create any relationship of agency, partnership, or joint venture between CNRI and Licensee. This License Agreement does not grant permission to use CNRI trademarks or trade name in a trademark sense to endorse or promote products or services of Licensee, or any third party.\n\n     8. By clicking on the \"ACCEPT\" button where indicated, or by copying, installing or otherwise using Python 1.6b1, Licensee agrees to be bound by the terms and conditions of this License Agreement.\n\nACCEPT\n\n\nCWI LICENSE AGREEMENT FOR PYTHON 0.9.0 THROUGH 1.2\n\nCopyright (c) 1991 - 1995, Stichting Mathematisch Centrum Amsterdam, The Netherlands. All rights reserved.\n\n     Permission to use, copy, modify, and distribute this software and its documentation for any purpose and without fee is hereby granted, provided that the above copyright notice appear in all copies and that both that copyright notice and this permission notice appear in supporting documentation, and that the name of Stichting Mathematisch Centrum or CWI not be used in advertising or publicity pertaining to distribution of the software without specific, written prior permission.\n\n     STICHTING MATHEMATISCH CENTRUM DISCLAIMS ALL WARRANTIES WITH REGARD TO THIS SOFTWARE, INCLUDING ALL IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY AND FITNESS, IN NO EVENT SHALL STICHTING MATHEMATISCH CENTRUM BE LIABLE FOR ANY SPECIAL, INDIRECT OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES OR ANY DAMAGES WHATSOEVER RESULTING FROM LOSS OF USE, DATA OR PROFITS, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, NEGLIGENCE OR OTHER TORTIOUS ACTION, ARISING OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE USE OR PERFORMANCE OF THIS SOFTWARE.', 'Python软件基础许可证版本2\n\n1.本许可协议由Python Software Foundation(以下简称PSF)与以源代码或二进制形式访问和使用本软件(简称《Python》)及其相关文档的个人或组织(简称被许可方)签订。\n\n2.根据本许可协议的条款和条件，PSF特此向被许可方授予非排他性、免版税、全球范围的许可，允许其复制、分析、测试、执行和/或公开展示、编写衍生作品、分发或以其他方式单独或以任何衍生版本使用Python，但前提是PSF的许可协议和PSF的版权声明，即“版权(C)2001、2002、2003、2004、2005、2006”保留在单独的Python或被许可方准备的任何衍生版本中。\n\n3.如果被许可方准备的派生作品是基于或合并了Python或其任何部分，并且希望按照本协议的规定将派生作品提供给其他人，则被许可方在此同意在任何此类作品中包含对Python所做更改的简要摘要。\n\n4.PSF正在“按原样”向被许可方提供Python。PSF不作任何明示或暗示的陈述或保证。举例来说，但不限于此，PSF对适销性或适用于任何特定目的或使用Python不会侵犯任何第三方权利的任何陈述或担保不作任何表示或保证。\n\n5.对于因修改、分发或以其他方式使用Python或其任何衍生产品而导致的任何附带、特殊或后果性的损害或损失，PSF不对被许可人或任何其他用户承担责任，即使已被告知可能发生这种情况。\n\n6.本许可协议将在严重违反其条款和条件时自动终止。\n\n7.本许可协议中的任何内容均不得被视为与PSF和被许可方之间的关系、伙伴关系或合资企业。本许可协议不允许在商标意义上使用PSF商标或商号来支持或推广被许可方或任何第三方的产品或服务。\n\n8.通过复制、安装或以其他方式使用Python，被许可方同意受本许可协议的条款和条件的约束。\n\n\nBEOPEN.COM关于Python2.0的许可协议\n\nBEOPEN Python开放源码许可协议版本1\n\n1.本许可协议由BeOpen.com(“BeOpen”)与以源代码或二进制形式访问和以其他方式使用本软件及其相关文档(“本软件”)的个人或组织(“被许可人”)签订，该网站的办公室位于加利福尼亚州圣克拉拉萨拉托加大道160号，邮编：95051。\n\n2.根据本BeOpen Python许可协议的条款和条件，BeOpen特此向被许可方授予非排他性、免版税、全球范围的许可，允许其复制、分析、测试、执行和/或公开展示、编写衍生作品、分发或以其他方式单独或以任何衍生版本使用软件，但前提是BeOpen Python许可仅保留在软件中或保留在被许可方准备的任何衍生版本中。\n\n3.BeOpen正在以“原样”的方式向被许可方提供软件。BEOPEN不作任何明示或暗示的陈述或保证。举例来说，但不限于此，BEOPEN对适销性或任何特定用途的适用性或使用软件不会侵犯任何第三方权利的陈述或担保不作任何表示或保证。\n\n4.对于因使用、修改或分发软件或其任何衍生产品而导致的任何附带、特殊或后果性的损害或损失，BEOPEN不对软件的被许可人或任何其他用户负责，即使被告知可能发生这种情况。\n\n5.本许可协议将在发生重大违规行为时自动终止TS条款和条件。\n\n6.本许可协议应在所有方面受加利福尼亚州法律管辖并由加利福尼亚州法律解释，但不包括法律冲突条款。本许可协议中的任何内容不得被视为在BeOpen和被许可方之间建立任何代理、合伙或合资关系。本许可协议不允许在商标意义上使用BeOpen商标或商号来支持或推广被许可方或任何第三方的产品或服务。作为例外，可以根据在该网页上授予的权限来使用http://www.pythonlabs.com/logos.html上提供的“BeOpen Python”徽标。\n\n7.通过复制、安装或以其他方式使用软件，被许可方同意受本许可协议的条款和条件的约束。\n\n\nCNRI开源许可协议(适用于Python1.6b1)\n\n重要提示：请仔细阅读以下协议。\n\n点击“接受”，或复制、安装或以其他方式使用Python1.6、测试版1软件，即表示您已同意本许可协议的条款和条件。\n\n1.本许可协议由总部设在弗吉尼亚州雷斯顿普雷斯顿怀特大道1895号的国家研究计划公司与访问和以其他方式使用源码或二进制形式的Python1.6、beta 1软件及其相关文档的个人或组织(被许可方)签订，该协议于2000年8月4日在www.python.org网站上发布(“Python1.6b1”)。\n\n2.根据本许可协议的条款和条件，CNRI特此向被许可方授予非独家、免版税、全球范围的许可，允许其公开复制、分析、测试、执行和/或展示、准备衍生作品、分发或以其他方式单独或在任何衍生版本中使用Python1.6b1，但前提是CNRI许可协议仅保留在Python1.6b1中或在任何衍生版本PREPA中保留被许可方为红色。\n\n或者，作为CNRI许可协议的替代，被许可方可以使用以下文本(省略引号)：“根据CNRIS许可协议中的条款和条件，可以使用Python1.6Beta1。本协议可以使用以下唯一的、持久的识别符(称为句柄)位于因特网上：1895.22/1011.本协议也可以使用URL从因特网上的代理服务器获得：http://hdl.handle.net/1895.22/1011”.\n\n3.如果被许可方准备了基于或结合了Python1.6b1或其任何部分的派生作品，并且希望按照本协议的规定向公众提供派生作品，则被许可方在此同意在任何此类作品中说明对Python1.6b1所做修改的性质。\n\n4.CNRI正在按“原样”向被许可方提供Python1.6b1。CNRI不作任何明示或暗示的陈述或保证。举个例子，但不限于，CNRI对适销性或适用于任何特定目的，或使用Python1.6b1不会侵犯任何第三方权利，不作任何陈述或保证。\n\n5.对于因使用、修改或分发Python1.6b1或其任何衍生产品而导致的任何附带、特殊或后果性的损害或损失，CNRI不对被许可人或软件的任何其他用户负责，即使被告知可能发生这种情况。\n\n6.本许可协议将在严重违反其条款和条件时自动终止。\n\n7.本许可协议应在所有方面受弗吉尼亚州法律管辖，并由弗吉尼亚州法律解释，不包括法律冲突条款。本许可协议中的任何内容不得被视为在CNRI和被许可方之间建立任何代理、合伙或合资关系。本许可协议未授权使用CNRI商标或商标意义上的商品名称来认可R推广被许可方或任何第三方的产品或服务。\n\n8.通过点击指定位置的“接受”按钮，或通过复制、安装或以其他方式使用Python1.6b1，被许可方同意受本许可协议的条款和条件的约束。\n\n接受\n\n\n从Python0.9.0到1.2的CWI许可协议\n\n版权所有(C)1991-1995，荷兰阿姆斯特丹数理中心。版权所有。\n\n特此授予为任何目的免费使用、复制、修改和分发本软件及其文档的许可，前提是上述版权声明出现在所有副本中，并且该版权声明和本许可声明均出现在支持文档中，并且未经事先明确的书面许可，不得在与软件分发相关的广告或宣传中使用Stichting Mahematich Centrum或CWI的名称。\n\nStichting MATHEMATISCH Centrum对本软件不作任何担保，包括对适销性和适用性的所有默示担保，在任何情况下，Stichting MATHEMATISCH Centrum均不对因使用或执行本软件而导致的任何特殊、间接或后果性损害或任何损害负责，无论是在合同诉讼、疏忽或其他侵权行为中。', 'This is the overall Python license, which is comprised of several licenses.');
INSERT INTO `license` VALUES (102, '2023-05-11 23:28:24', 'ZPL-2.0', 'Zope Public License 2.0', 'http://old.zope.org/Resources/License/ZPL-2.0,https://opensource.org/licenses/ZPL-2.0', 0, 0, 1, 1, NULL, '<<beginOptional>> Zope Public License (ZPL) Version 2.0<<endOptional>> <<var;name=\"copyright\";original=\"This software is Copyright (c) Zope Corporation (tm) and Contributors. All rights reserved.\";match=\".{0,1000}\">><<beginOptional>> This license has been certified as open source. It has also been designated as GPL compatible by the Free Software Foundation (FSF).<<endOptional>>\n\nRedistribution and use in source and binary forms, with or without modification, are permitted provided that the following conditions are met:\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Redistributions in source code must retain the above copyright notice, this list of conditions, and the following disclaimer.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"2.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Redistributions in binary form must reproduce the above copyright notice, this list of conditions, and the following disclaimer in the documentation and/or other materials provided with the distribution.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"3.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> The name Zope Corporation (tm) must not be used to endorse or promote products derived from this software without prior written permission from Zope Corporation.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"4.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> The right to distribute this software or to use it for any purpose does not give you the right to use Servicemarks (sm) or Trademarks (tm) of Zope Corporation. Use of them is covered in a separate agreement (see http://www.zope.com/Marks).\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"5.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> If any files are modified, you must cause the modified files to carry prominent notices stating that you changed the files and the date of any change.\n\nDisclaimer\n\nTHIS SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED BY ZOPE CORPORATION ``AS IS\'\' AND ANY EXPRESSED OR IMPLIED WARRANTIES, INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, THE IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY AND FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE ARE DISCLAIMED. IN NO EVENT SHALL ZOPE CORPORATION OR ITS CONTRIBUTORS BE LIABLE FOR ANY DIRECT, INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, EXEMPLARY, OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES (INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, PROCUREMENT OF SUBSTITUTE GOODS OR SERVICES; LOSS OF USE, DATA, OR PROFITS; OR BUSINESS INTERRUPTION) HOWEVER CAUSED AND ON ANY THEORY OF LIABILITY, WHETHER IN CONTRACT, STRICT LIABILITY, OR TORT (INCLUDING NEGLIGENCE OR OTHERWISE) ARISING IN ANY WAY OUT OF THE USE OF THIS SOFTWARE, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGE.<<beginOptional>> This software consists of contributions made by Zope Corporation and many individuals on behalf of Zope Corporation. Specific attributions are listed in the accompanying credits file.<<endOptional>>', 'Zope Public License (ZPL) Version 2.0\n\nThis software is Copyright (c) Zope Corporation (tm) and Contributors. All rights reserved.\n\nThis license has been certified as open source. It has also been designated as GPL compatible by the Free Software Foundation (FSF).\n\nRedistribution and use in source and binary forms, with or without modification, are permitted provided that the following conditions are met:\n\n     1. Redistributions in source code must retain the above copyright notice, this list of conditions, and the following disclaimer.\n\n     2. Redistributions in binary form must reproduce the above copyright notice, this list of conditions, and the following disclaimer in the documentation and/or other materials provided with the distribution.\n\n     3. The name Zope Corporation (tm) must not be used to endorse or promote products derived from this software without prior written permission from Zope Corporation.\n\n     4. The right to distribute this software or to use it for any purpose does not give you the right to use Servicemarks (sm) or Trademarks (tm) of Zope Corporation. Use of them is covered in a separate agreement (see http://www.zope.com/Marks).\n\n     5. If any files are modified, you must cause the modified files to carry prominent notices stating that you changed the files and the date of any change.\n\nDisclaimer\n\nTHIS SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED BY ZOPE CORPORATION ``AS IS\'\' AND ANY EXPRESSED OR IMPLIED WARRANTIES, INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, THE IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY AND FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE ARE DISCLAIMED.  IN NO EVENT SHALL ZOPE CORPORATION OR ITS CONTRIBUTORS BE LIABLE FOR ANY DIRECT, INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, EXEMPLARY, OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES (INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, PROCUREMENT OF SUBSTITUTE GOODS OR SERVICES; LOSS OF USE, DATA, OR PROFITS; OR BUSINESS INTERRUPTION) HOWEVER CAUSED AND ON ANY THEORY OF LIABILITY, WHETHER IN CONTRACT, STRICT LIABILITY, OR TORT (INCLUDING NEGLIGENCE OR OTHERWISE) ARISING IN ANY WAY OUT OF THE USE OF THIS SOFTWARE, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGE.\n\nThis software consists of contributions made by Zope Corporation and many individuals on behalf of Zope Corporation.  Specific attributions are listed in the accompanying credits file.', 'Zope公共许可证(ZPL)2.0版\n\n本软件版权所有(C)Zope Corporation(Tm)及其贡献者。版权所有。\n\n此许可证已被认证为开放源码。它还被自由软件基金会(FSF)指定为与GPL兼容。\n\n在满足以下条件的情况下，允许以源代码和二进制形式重新分发和使用，无论是否进行修改：\n\n1.源代码中的再分发必须保留上述版权声明、此条件列表和以下免责声明。\n\n2.二进制形式的再分发必须在随分发提供的文档和/或其他材料中复制上述版权声明、此条件列表和以下免责声明。\n\n3.未经Zope Corporation事先书面许可，不得使用Zope Corporation(Tm)的名称来支持或促销从本软件派生的产品。\n\n4.分发本软件或将其用于任何目的的权利并不授予您使用Zope Corporation的服务标记(Sm)或商标(Tm)的权利。它们的使用包含在单独的协议中(请参阅http://www.zope.com/Marks).\n\n5.如果修改了任何文件，您必须使修改后的文件带有显眼的通知，说明您更改了文件和任何更改的日期。\n\n免责\n\n本软件由Zope Corporation“按原样”提供，拒绝提供任何明示或默示的保证，包括但不限于对适销性和特定用途适用性的默示保证。在任何情况下，Zope Corporation或其贡献者都不对任何直接、间接、附带、特殊、惩罚性或后果性的损害(包括但不限于替代商品或服务的采购；使用、数据或利润的损失；或业务中断)承担任何责任，无论是合同责任、严格责任或侵权行为(包括疏忽或其他)停止使用本软件，即使被告知可能会受到此类损害。\n\n该软件由Zope公司和许多代表Zope公司的个人贡献而成。具体的归属列在随附的制作者名单文件中。', NULL);
INSERT INTO `license` VALUES (103, '2023-05-11 23:28:24', 'GPL-2.0-with-GCC-exception', 'GNU General Public License v2.0 w/GCC Runtime Library exception', 'https://gcc.gnu.org/git/?p=gcc.git;a=blob;f=gcc/libgcc1.c;h=762f5143fc6eed57b6797c82710f3538aa52b40b;hb=cb143a3ce4fb417c68f5fa2691a1b1b1053dfba9#l10', 0, 1, 0, 0, NULL, 'insert GPL v2 license text here\n\nGCC Linking Exception\n\nIn addition to the permissions in the GNU General Public License, the Free Software Foundation gives you unlimited permission to link the compiled version of this file into combinations with other programs, and to distribute those combinations without any restriction coming from the use of this file. (The General Public License restrictions do apply in other respects; for example, they cover modification of the file, and distribution when not linked into a combine executable.', 'insert GPL v2 license text here\n\nGCC Linking Exception\n\nIn addition to the permissions in the GNU General Public License, the Free Software Foundation gives you unlimited permission to link the compiled version of this file into combinations with other programs, and to distribute those combinations without any restriction coming from the use of this file. (The General Public License restrictions do apply in other respects; for example, they cover modification of the file, and distribution when not linked into a combine executable.', '在此处插入GPL v2许可证文本\n\nGCC链接异常\n\n除了GNU通用公共许可证中的权限，自由软件基金会还授予您无限的权限，可以将此文件的编译版本链接到与其他程序的组合中，并分发这些组合，而不会因使用此文件而受到任何限制。(通用公共许可证限制确实适用于其他方面；例如，它们涵盖对文件的修改，以及未链接到联合可执行文件时的分发。', NULL);
INSERT INTO `license` VALUES (104, '2023-05-11 23:28:24', 'Artistic-1.0', 'Artistic License 1.0', 'https://opensource.org/licenses/Artistic-1.0', 0, 0, 1, 0, NULL, '<<beginOptional>> The Artistic License<<endOptional>>\n\nPreamble\n\nThe intent of this document is to state the conditions under which a Package may be copied, such that the Copyright Holder maintains some semblance of artistic control over the development of the package, while giving the users of the package the right to use and distribute the Package in a more-or-less customary fashion, plus the right to make reasonable modifications.\n\nDefinitions:\n\n\"Package\" refers to the collection of files distributed by the Copyright Holder, and derivatives of that collection of files created through textual modification.\n\n\"Standard Version\" refers to such a Package if it has not been modified, or has been modified in accordance with the wishes of the Copyright Holder.\n\n\"Copyright Holder\" is whoever is named in the copyright or copyrights for the package.\n\n\"You\" is you, if you\'re thinking about copying or distributing this Package.\n\n\"Reasonable copying fee\" is whatever you can justify on the basis of media cost, duplication charges, time of people involved, and so on. (You will not be required to justify it to the Copyright Holder, but only to the computing community at large as a market that must bear the fee.)\n\n\"Freely Available\" means that no fee is charged for the item itself, though there may be fees involved in handling the item. It also means that recipients of the item may redistribute it under the same conditions they received it.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> You may make and give away verbatim copies of the source form of the Standard Version of this Package without restriction, provided that you duplicate all of the original copyright notices and associated disclaimers.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"2.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> You may apply bug fixes, portability fixes and other modifications derived from the Public Domain or from the Copyright Holder. A Package modified in such a way shall still be considered the Standard Version.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"3.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> You may otherwise modify your copy of this Package in any way, provided that you insert a prominent notice in each changed file stating how and when you changed that file, and provided that you do at least ONE of the following:\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"a)\";match=\".{0,20}\">> place your modifications in the Public Domain or otherwise make them Freely Available, such as by posting said modifications to Usenet or an equivalent medium, or placing the modifications on a major archive site such as ftp.uu.net, or by allowing the Copyright Holder to include your modifications in the Standard Version of the Package.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"b)\";match=\".{0,20}\">> use the modified Package only within your corporation or organization.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"c)\";match=\".{0,20}\">> rename any non-standard executables so the names do not conflict with standard executables, which must also be provided, and provide a separate manual page for each non-standard executable that clearly documents how it differs from the Standard Version.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"d)\";match=\".{0,20}\">> make other distribution arrangements with the Copyright Holder.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"4.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> You may distribute the programs of this Package in object code or executable form, provided that you do at least ONE of the following:\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"a)\";match=\".{0,20}\">> distribute a Standard Version of the executables and library files, together with instructions (in the manual page or equivalent) on where to get the Standard Version.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"b)\";match=\".{0,20}\">> accompany the distribution with the machine-readable source of the Package with your modifications.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"c)\";match=\".{0,20}\">> accompany any non-standard executables with their corresponding Standard Version executables, giving the non-standard executables non-standard names, and clearly documenting the differences in manual pages (or equivalent), together with instructions on where to get the Standard Version.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"d)\";match=\".{0,20}\">> make other distribution arrangements with the Copyright Holder.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"5.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> You may charge a reasonable copying fee for any distribution of this Package. You may charge any fee you choose for support of this Package. You may not charge a fee for this Package itself. However, you may distribute this Package in aggregate with other (possibly commercial) programs as part of a larger (possibly commercial) software distribution provided that you do not advertise this Package as a product of your own.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"6.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> The scripts and library files supplied as input to or produced as output from the programs of this Package do not automatically fall under the copyright of this Package, but belong to whomever generated them, and may be sold commercially, and may be aggregated with this Package.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"7.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> C or perl subroutines supplied by you and linked into this Package shall not be considered part of this Package.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"8.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> The name of the Copyright Holder may not be used to endorse or promote products derived from this software without specific prior written permission.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"9.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> THIS PACKAGE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\" AND WITHOUT ANY EXPRESS OR IMPLIED WARRANTIES, INCLUDING, WITHOUT LIMITATION, THE IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTIBILITY AND FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.<<beginOptional>> The End<<endOptional>>', 'The Artistic License\n\nPreamble\n\nThe intent of this document is to state the conditions under which a Package may be copied, such that the Copyright Holder maintains some semblance of artistic control over the development of the package, while giving the users of the package the right to use and distribute the Package in a more-or-less customary fashion, plus the right to make reasonable modifications.\n\nDefinitions:\n\n     \"Package\" refers to the collection of files distributed by the Copyright Holder, and derivatives of that collection of files created through textual modification.\n\n     \"Standard Version\" refers to such a Package if it has not been modified, or has been modified in accordance with the wishes of the Copyright Holder.\n\n     \"Copyright Holder\" is whoever is named in the copyright or copyrights for the package.\n\n     \"You\" is you, if you\'re thinking about copying or distributing this Package.\n\n     \"Reasonable copying fee\" is whatever you can justify on the basis of media cost, duplication charges, time of people involved, and so on. (You will not be required to justify it to the Copyright Holder, but only to the computing community at large as a market that must bear the fee.)\n\n     \"Freely Available\" means that no fee is charged for the item itself, though there may be fees involved in handling the item. It also means that recipients of the item may redistribute it under the same conditions they received it.\n\n1. You may make and give away verbatim copies of the source form of the Standard Version of this Package without restriction, provided that you duplicate all of the original copyright notices and associated disclaimers.\n\n2. You may apply bug fixes, portability fixes and other modifications derived from the Public Domain or from the Copyright Holder. A Package modified in such a way shall still be considered the Standard Version.\n\n3. You may otherwise modify your copy of this Package in any way, provided that you insert a prominent notice in each changed file stating how and when you changed that file, and provided that you do at least ONE of the following:\n\n     a) place your modifications in the Public Domain or otherwise make them Freely Available, such as by posting said modifications to Usenet or an equivalent medium, or placing the modifications on a major archive site such as ftp.uu.net, or by allowing the Copyright Holder to include your modifications in the Standard Version of the Package.\n     b) use the modified Package only within your corporation or organization.\n     c) rename any non-standard executables so the names do not conflict with standard executables, which must also be provided, and provide a separate manual page for each non-standard executable that clearly documents how it differs from the Standard Version.\n     d) make other distribution arrangements with the Copyright Holder.\n\n4. You may distribute the programs of this Package in object code or executable form, provided that you do at least ONE of the following:\n\n     a) distribute a Standard Version of the executables and library files, together with instructions (in the manual page or equivalent) on where to get the Standard Version.\n     b) accompany the distribution with the machine-readable source of the Package with your modifications.\n     c) accompany any non-standard executables with their corresponding Standard Version executables, giving the non-standard executables non-standard names, and clearly documenting the differences in manual pages (or equivalent), together with instructions on where to get the Standard Version.\n     d) make other distribution arrangements with the Copyright Holder.\n\n5. You may charge a reasonable copying fee for any distribution of this Package. You may charge any fee you choose for support of this Package. You may not charge a fee for this Package itself. However, you may distribute this Package in aggregate with other (possibly commercial) programs as part of a larger (possibly commercial) software distribution provided that you do not advertise this Package as a product of your own.\n\n6. The scripts and library files supplied as input to or produced as output from the programs of this Package do not automatically fall under the copyright of this Package, but belong to whomever generated them, and may be sold commercially, and may be aggregated with this Package.\n\n7. C or perl subroutines supplied by you and linked into this Package shall not be considered part of this Package.\n\n8. The name of the Copyright Holder may not be used to endorse or promote products derived from this software without specific prior written permission.\n\n9. THIS PACKAGE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\" AND WITHOUT ANY EXPRESS OR IMPLIED WARRANTIES, INCLUDING, WITHOUT LIMITATION, THE IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTIBILITY AND FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.\n\nThe End', '艺术许可\n\n前言\n\n本文档的目的是说明可以复制包的条件，以便版权所有者对包的开发保持某种表面上的艺术控制，同时给予包的用户以或多或少的习惯方式使用和分发包的权利，以及进行合理修改的权利。\n\n定义：\n\n“包”是指版权所有者分发的文件的集合，以及通过文本修改创建的该文件集合的衍生品。\n\n“标准版本”是指未经修改或已根据版权所有者的意愿进行修改的包。\n\n“版权所有者”是在包的一个或多个版权中指定的任何人。\n\n“你”就是你，如果你想复制或分发这个包的话。\n\n“合理的复制费”是指根据媒体成本、复制费、涉及人员的时间等来证明合理的复制费。(你不需要向版权所有者证明这一点，只需要向整个计算社区证明，这是一个必须承担费用的市场。)\n\n“免费可用”是指不收取物品本身的费用，尽管在处理物品时可能会收取费用。这还意味着，物品的接收者可以在与收到物品相同的条件下重新分发物品。\n\n1.您可以不受限制地制作和分发本程序包标准版本的源格式的逐字副本，前提是您必须复制所有原始版权声明和相关免责声明。\n\n2.您可以应用来自公共领域或版权所有者的错误修复、可移植性修复和其他修改。以这种方式修改的包仍应被视为标准版本。\n\n3.您可以以其他方式修改您的本包副本，前提是您在每个已更改的文件，说明您更改该文件的方式和时间，并假设您至少执行以下操作之一：\n\nA)将您的修改放在公共领域或以其他方式免费提供，例如通过将所述修改发布到Usenet或同等媒体，或将修改放在主要归档网站(如ftp.uu.net)上，或允许版权所有者将您的修改包括在包的标准版本中。\nB)仅在您的公司或组织内使用修改后的包。\nC)重命名任何非标准可执行文件，使其名称不与标准可执行文件冲突，标准可执行文件也必须提供，并为每个非标准可执行文件提供单独的手册页，清楚地记录它与标准版本的区别。\nD)与版权持有人作出其他分发安排。\n\n4.您可以以目标代码或可执行文件的形式分发本程序包中的程序，前提是您至少执行以下操作之一：\n\nA)分发可执行文件和库文件的标准版本，以及关于从哪里获取标准版本的说明(在手册页或同等内容中)。\nB)随包的机器可读源代码以及您的修改一起分发。\nC)将任何非标准可执行文件与其相应的标准版本可执行文件一起使用，为非标准可执行文件指定非标准名称，并在手册页(或同等文件)中清楚地记录不同之处，以及从哪里获得标准版本的说明。\nD)与版权持有人作出其他分发安排。\n\n5.您可以就本套餐的任何分发收取合理的复印费。您可以收取您选择的任何费用来支持此套餐。您不能对此套餐本身收取费用。但是，您可以将此包与其他(可能是商业的)程序一起分发，作为更大的(可能是商业的)S的一部分软件分发，前提是您不要将此程序包宣传为您自己的产品。\n\n6.作为本包程序的输入或输出提供的脚本和库文件不自动属于本包的版权，但属于生成它们的任何人，可以商业销售，也可以与本包合并。\n\n7.由您提供并链接到此程序包的C或Perl子例程不应被视为此程序包的一部分。\n\n8.未经事先明确的书面许可，不得使用版权所有者的名称为本软件衍生的产品代言或促销。\n\n9.本产品包按原样提供，不提供任何明示或默示保证，包括但不限于对MERCHANTILITY和是否适合特定目的的默示保证。\n\n结束', 'This license was superseded by v2.0. This is Artistic License 1.0 as found on OSI site, excluding clause 8.');
INSERT INTO `license` VALUES (105, '2023-05-11 23:28:24', 'CERN-OHL-P-2.0', 'CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - Permissive', 'https://www.ohwr.org/project/cernohl/wikis/Documents/CERN-OHL-version-2', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, '<<beginOptional>> CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - Permissive<<endOptional>>\n\nPreamble\n\nCERN has developed this licence to promote collaboration among hardware designers and to provide a legal tool which supports the freedom to use, study, modify, share and distribute hardware designs and products based on those designs. Version 2 of the CERN Open Hardware Licence comes in three variants: this licence, CERN-OHL-P (permissive); and two reciprocal licences: CERN- OHL-W (weakly reciprocal) and CERN-OHL-S (strongly reciprocal).\n\nThe CERN-OHL-P is copyright CERN 2020. Anyone is welcome to use it, in unmodified form only.\n\nUse of this Licence does not imply any endorsement by CERN of any Licensor or their designs nor does it imply any involvement by CERN in their development.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Definitions\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.1\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \'Licence\' means this CERN-OHL-P.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.2\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \'Source\' means information such as design materials or digital code which can be applied to Make or test a Product or to prepare a Product for use, Conveyance or sale, regardless of its medium or how it is expressed. It may include Notices.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.3\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \'Covered Source\' means Source that is explicitly made available under this Licence.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.4\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \'Product\' means any device, component, work or physical object, whether in finished or intermediate form, arising from the use, application or processing of Covered Source.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.5\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \'Make\' means to create or configure something, whether by manufacture, assembly, compiling, loading or applying Covered Source or another Product or otherwise.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.6\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \'Notice\' means copyright, acknowledgement and trademark notices, references to the location of any Notices, modification notices (subsection 3.3(b)) and all notices that refer to this Licence and to the disclaimer of warranties that are included in the Covered Source.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.7\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \'Licensee\' or \'You\' means any person exercising rights under this Licence.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.8\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \'Licensor\' means a person who creates Source or modifies Covered Source and subsequently Conveys the resulting Covered Source under the terms and conditions of this Licence. A person may be a Licensee and a Licensor at the same time.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.9\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \'Convey\' means to communicate to the public or distribute.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"2\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Applicability\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"2.1\";match=\".{0,20}\">> This Licence governs the use, copying, modification, Conveying of Covered Source and Products, and the Making of Products. By exercising any right granted under this Licence, You irrevocably accept these terms and conditions.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"2.2\";match=\".{0,20}\">> This Licence is granted by the Licensor directly to You, and shall apply worldwide and without limitation in time.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"2.3\";match=\".{0,20}\">> You shall not attempt to restrict by contract or otherwise the rights granted under this Licence to other Licensees.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"2.4\";match=\".{0,20}\">> This Licence is not intended to restrict fair use, fair dealing, or any other similar right.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"3\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Copying, modifying and Conveying Covered Source\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"3.1\";match=\".{0,20}\">> You may copy and Convey verbatim copies of Covered Source, in any medium, provided You retain all Notices.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"3.2\";match=\".{0,20}\">> You may modify Covered Source, other than Notices.\n\n      You may only delete Notices if they are no longer applicable to the corresponding Covered Source as modified by You and You may add additional Notices applicable to Your modifications.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"3.3\";match=\".{0,20}\">> You may Convey modified Covered Source (with the effect that You shall also become a Licensor) provided that You:\n\n         <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"a)\";match=\".{0,20}\">> retain Notices as required in subsection 3.2; and\n\n         <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"b)\";match=\".{0,20}\">> add a Notice to the modified Covered Source stating that You have modified it, with the date and brief description of how You have modified it.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"3.4\";match=\".{0,20}\">> You may Convey Covered Source or modified Covered Source under licence terms which differ from the terms of this Licence provided that:\n\n         <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"a)\";match=\".{0,20}\">> You comply at all times with subsection 3.3; and\n\n         <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"b)\";match=\".{0,20}\">> You provide a copy of this Licence to anyone to whom You Convey Covered Source or modified Covered Source.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"4\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Making and Conveying Products\n\n   You may Make Products, and/or Convey them, provided that You ensure that the recipient of the Product has access to any Notices applicable to the Product.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"5\";match=\".{0,20}\">> DISCLAIMER AND LIABILITY\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"5.1\";match=\".{0,20}\">> DISCLAIMER OF WARRANTY -- The Covered Source and any Products are provided \'as is\' and any express or implied warranties, including, but not limited to, implied warranties of merchantability, of satisfactory quality, non-infringement of third party rights, and fitness for a particular purpose or use are disclaimed in respect of any Source or Product to the maximum extent permitted by law. The Licensor makes no representation that any Source or Product does not or will not infringe any patent, copyright, trade secret or other proprietary right. The entire risk as to the use, quality, and performance of any Source or Product shall be with You and not the Licensor. This disclaimer of warranty is an essential part of this Licence and a condition for the grant of any rights granted under this Licence.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"5.2\";match=\".{0,20}\">> EXCLUSION AND LIMITATION OF LIABILITY -- The Licensor shall, to the maximum extent permitted by law, have no liability for direct, indirect, special, incidental, consequential, exemplary, punitive or other damages of any character including, without limitation, procurement of substitute goods or services, loss of use, data or profits, or business interruption, however caused and on any theory of contract, warranty, tort (including negligence), product liability or otherwise, arising in any way in relation to the Covered Source, modified Covered Source and/or the Making or Conveyance of a Product, even if advised of the possibility of such damages, and You shall hold the Licensor(s) free and harmless from any liability, costs, damages, fees and expenses, including claims by third parties, in relation to such use.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"6\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Patents\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"6.1\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Subject to the terms and conditions of this Licence, each Licensor hereby grants to You a perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive, no-charge, royalty-free, irrevocable (except as stated in this section 6, or where terminated by the Licensor for cause) patent license to Make, have Made, use, offer to sell, sell, import, and otherwise transfer the Covered Source and Products, where such licence applies only to those patent claims licensable by such Licensor that are necessarily infringed by exercising rights under the Covered Source as Conveyed by that Licensor.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"6.2\";match=\".{0,20}\">> If You institute patent litigation against any entity (including a cross-claim or counterclaim in a lawsuit) alleging that the Covered Source or a Product constitutes direct or contributory patent infringement, or You seek any declaration that a patent licensed to You under this Licence is invalid or unenforceable then any rights granted to You under this Licence shall terminate as of the date such process is initiated.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"7\";match=\".{0,20}\">> General\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"7.1\";match=\".{0,20}\">> If any provisions of this Licence are or subsequently become invalid or unenforceable for any reason, the remaining provisions shall remain effective.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"7.2\";match=\".{0,20}\">> You shall not use any of the name (including acronyms and abbreviations), image, or logo by which the Licensor or CERN is known, except where needed to comply with section 3, or where the use is otherwise allowed by law. Any such permitted use shall be factual and shall not be made so as to suggest any kind of endorsement or implication of involvement by the Licensor or its personnel.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"7.3\";match=\".{0,20}\">> CERN may publish updated versions and variants of this Licence which it considers to be in the spirit of this version, but may differ in detail to address new problems or concerns. New versions will be published with a unique version number and a variant identifier specifying the variant. If the Licensor has specified that a given variant applies to the Covered Source without specifying a version, You may treat that Covered Source as being released under any version of the CERN-OHL with that variant. If no variant is specified, the Covered Source shall be treated as being released under CERN-OHL-S. The Licensor may also specify that the Covered Source is subject to a specific version of the CERN-OHL or any later version in which case You may apply this or any later version of CERN-OHL with the same variant identifier published by CERN.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"7.4\";match=\".{0,20}\">> This Licence shall not be enforceable except by a Licensor acting as such, and third party beneficiary rights are specifically excluded.', 'CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - Permissive\n\n\nPreamble\n\nCERN has developed this licence to promote collaboration among\nhardware designers and to provide a legal tool which supports the\nfreedom to use, study, modify, share and distribute hardware designs\nand products based on those designs. Version 2 of the CERN Open\nHardware Licence comes in three variants: this licence, CERN-OHL-P\n(permissive); and two reciprocal licences: CERN- OHL-W (weakly\nreciprocal) and CERN-OHL-S (strongly reciprocal).\n\nThe CERN-OHL-P is copyright CERN 2020. Anyone is welcome to use it, in\nunmodified form only.\n\nUse of this Licence does not imply any endorsement by CERN of any\nLicensor or their designs nor does it imply any involvement by CERN in\ntheir development.\n\n\n1 Definitions\n\n  1.1 \'Licence\' means this CERN-OHL-P.\n\n  1.2 \'Source\' means information such as design materials or digital\n      code which can be applied to Make or test a Product or to\n      prepare a Product for use, Conveyance or sale, regardless of its\n      medium or how it is expressed. It may include Notices.\n\n  1.3 \'Covered Source\' means Source that is explicitly made available\n      under this Licence.\n\n  1.4 \'Product\' means any device, component, work or physical object,\n      whether in finished or intermediate form, arising from the use,\n      application or processing of Covered Source.\n\n  1.5 \'Make\' means to create or configure something, whether by\n     manufacture, assembly, compiling, loading or applying Covered\n     Source or another Product or otherwise.\n\n  1.6 \'Notice\' means copyright, acknowledgement and trademark notices,\n      references to the location of any Notices, modification notices\n      (subsection 3.3(b)) and all notices that refer to this Licence\n      and to the disclaimer of warranties that are included in the\n      Covered Source.\n\n  1.7 \'Licensee\' or \'You\' means any person exercising rights under\n      this Licence.\n\n  1.8 \'Licensor\' means a person who creates Source or modifies Covered\n      Source and subsequently Conveys the resulting Covered Source\n      under the terms and conditions of this Licence. A person may be\n      a Licensee and a Licensor at the same time.\n\n  1.9 \'Convey\' means to communicate to the public or distribute.\n\n\n2 Applicability\n\n  2.1 This Licence governs the use, copying, modification, Conveying\n      of Covered Source and Products, and the Making of Products. By\n      exercising any right granted under this Licence, You irrevocably\n      accept these terms and conditions.\n\n  2.2 This Licence is granted by the Licensor directly to You, and\n      shall apply worldwide and without limitation in time.\n\n  2.3 You shall not attempt to restrict by contract or otherwise the\n      rights granted under this Licence to other Licensees.\n\n  2.4 This Licence is not intended to restrict fair use, fair dealing,\n      or any other similar right.\n\n\n3 Copying, modifying and Conveying Covered Source\n\n  3.1 You may copy and Convey verbatim copies of Covered Source, in\n      any medium, provided You retain all Notices.\n\n  3.2 You may modify Covered Source, other than Notices.\n\n      You may only delete Notices if they are no longer applicable to\n      the corresponding Covered Source as modified by You and You may\n      add additional Notices applicable to Your modifications.\n\n  3.3 You may Convey modified Covered Source (with the effect that You\n      shall also become a Licensor) provided that You:\n\n       a) retain Notices as required in subsection 3.2; and\n\n       b) add a Notice to the modified Covered Source stating that You\n          have modified it, with the date and brief description of how\n          You have modified it.\n\n  3.4 You may Convey Covered Source or modified Covered Source under\n      licence terms which differ from the terms of this Licence\n      provided that:\n\n       a) You comply at all times with subsection 3.3; and\n\n       b) You provide a copy of this Licence to anyone to whom You\n          Convey Covered Source or modified Covered Source.\n\n\n4 Making and Conveying Products\n\nYou may Make Products, and/or Convey them, provided that You ensure\nthat the recipient of the Product has access to any Notices applicable\nto the Product.\n\n\n5 DISCLAIMER AND LIABILITY\n\n  5.1 DISCLAIMER OF WARRANTY -- The Covered Source and any Products\n      are provided \'as is\' and any express or implied warranties,\n      including, but not limited to, implied warranties of\n      merchantability, of satisfactory quality, non-infringement of\n      third party rights, and fitness for a particular purpose or use\n      are disclaimed in respect of any Source or Product to the\n      maximum extent permitted by law. The Licensor makes no\n      representation that any Source or Product does not or will not\n      infringe any patent, copyright, trade secret or other\n      proprietary right. The entire risk as to the use, quality, and\n      performance of any Source or Product shall be with You and not\n      the Licensor. This disclaimer of warranty is an essential part\n      of this Licence and a condition for the grant of any rights\n      granted under this Licence.\n\n  5.2 EXCLUSION AND LIMITATION OF LIABILITY -- The Licensor shall, to\n      the maximum extent permitted by law, have no liability for\n      direct, indirect, special, incidental, consequential, exemplary,\n      punitive or other damages of any character including, without\n      limitation, procurement of substitute goods or services, loss of\n      use, data or profits, or business interruption, however caused\n      and on any theory of contract, warranty, tort (including\n      negligence), product liability or otherwise, arising in any way\n      in relation to the Covered Source, modified Covered Source\n      and/or the Making or Conveyance of a Product, even if advised of\n      the possibility of such damages, and You shall hold the\n      Licensor(s) free and harmless from any liability, costs,\n      damages, fees and expenses, including claims by third parties,\n      in relation to such use.\n\n\n6 Patents\n\n  6.1 Subject to the terms and conditions of this Licence, each\n      Licensor hereby grants to You a perpetual, worldwide,\n      non-exclusive, no-charge, royalty-free, irrevocable (except as\n      stated in this section 6, or where terminated by the Licensor\n      for cause) patent license to Make, have Made, use, offer to\n      sell, sell, import, and otherwise transfer the Covered Source\n      and Products, where such licence applies only to those patent\n      claims licensable by such Licensor that are necessarily\n      infringed by exercising rights under the Covered Source as\n      Conveyed by that Licensor.\n\n  6.2 If You institute patent litigation against any entity (including\n      a cross-claim or counterclaim in a lawsuit) alleging that the\n      Covered Source or a Product constitutes direct or contributory\n      patent infringement, or You seek any declaration that a patent\n      licensed to You under this Licence is invalid or unenforceable\n      then any rights granted to You under this Licence shall\n      terminate as of the date such process is initiated.\n\n\n7 General\n\n  7.1 If any provisions of this Licence are or subsequently become\n      invalid or unenforceable for any reason, the remaining\n      provisions shall remain effective.\n\n  7.2 You shall not use any of the name (including acronyms and\n      abbreviations), image, or logo by which the Licensor or CERN is\n      known, except where needed to comply with section 3, or where\n      the use is otherwise allowed by law. Any such permitted use\n      shall be factual and shall not be made so as to suggest any kind\n      of endorsement or implication of involvement by the Licensor or\n      its personnel.\n\n  7.3 CERN may publish updated versions and variants of this Licence\n      which it considers to be in the spirit of this version, but may\n      differ in detail to address new problems or concerns. New\n      versions will be published with a unique version number and a\n      variant identifier specifying the variant. If the Licensor has\n      specified that a given variant applies to the Covered Source\n      without specifying a version, You may treat that Covered Source\n      as being released under any version of the CERN-OHL with that\n      variant. If no variant is specified, the Covered Source shall be\n      treated as being released under CERN-OHL-S. The Licensor may\n      also specify that the Covered Source is subject to a specific\n      version of the CERN-OHL or any later version in which case You\n      may apply this or any later version of CERN-OHL with the same\n      variant identifier published by CERN.\n\n  7.4 This Licence shall not be enforceable except by a Licensor\n      acting as such, and third party beneficiary rights are\n      specifically excluded.', 'CERN开放硬件许可证版本2-许可\n\n\n前言\n\n欧洲核子研究中心开发了这一许可证，以促进\n并提供支持硬件设计的法律工具\n自由使用、研究、修改、共享和分发硬件设计\n以及基于这些设计的产品。欧洲核子研究中心公开赛第二版\n硬件许可证有三种变体：此许可证，CERN-OHL-P\n(许可)；和两个相互的许可证：CERN-OHL-W(弱\n倒易)和CERN-OHL-S(强互易)。\n\nCERN-OHL-P版权所有CERN 2020。欢迎任何人使用它，在\n仅限未修改的形式。\n\n使用本许可证并不意味着欧洲核子研究中心对任何\n许可方或他们的设计，也不暗示CERN参与\n他们的发展。\n\n\n1定义\n\n1.1“许可证”是指本CERN-OHL-P。\n\n1.2来源是指设计材料或数字等信息\n可用于制造或测试产品或\n准备产品以供使用、运输或销售，而不考虑其\n媒介或它的表达方式。它可能包括通知。\n\n1.3“被覆盖来源”是指明确提供的来源\n根据本牌照。\n\n1.4“产品”是指任何设备、部件、工作或实物，\n无论是成品形式还是中间形式，在使用过程中，\n承保来源的申请或处理。\n\n1.5‘make’的意思是创建或配置某物，无论是通过\n包括制造、组装、编译、装载或应用\n来源或其他产品或其他。\n\n1.6“通知”系指版权、确认书和商标通知，\n对任何通知、修改通知\n(第3.3(B)款)及所有提及本牌照的告示\n和对包含在\n覆盖来源。\n\n1.7“被许可人”或“您”指任何行使下列权利的人\n本牌照。\n\n1.8“许可人”是指创建源或修改封面的人边\n来源，并随后传送所产生的覆盖来源\n根据本牌照的条款及条件。一个人可能是\n同时作为被许可方和许可方。\n\n1.9“传达”是指向公众传达或分发。\n\n\n2适用性\n\n2.1本牌照规管使用、复制、修改、传送\n涵盖的来源和产品，以及产品的制造。通过\n行使根据本许可证授予的任何权利，您不可撤销\n接受这些条款和条件。\n\n2.2本许可证由许可方直接授予您，并且\n应在全球范围内且不受时间限制地适用。\n\n2.3您不得试图通过合同或其他方式限制\n根据本许可证授予其他被许可人的权利。\n\n2.4本许可证的目的不是限制合理使用、公平交易、\n或任何其他类似的权利。\n\n\n3复制、修改和传达所涵盖的来源\n\n3.1您可以在以下位置复制和传达所涵盖源代码的逐字副本\n任何媒介，只要你保留所有通知。\n\n3.2除通知外，您可以修改承保来源。\n\n您只能删除不再适用于以下内容的通知\n由您修改的相应的承保来源，您可能\n添加适用于您的修改的其他通知。\n\n3.3您可以传达经修改的承保来源(效果是您\n也应成为许可方)，前提是您：\n\nA)保留第3.2款规定的通知；和\n\nB)在修改的承保来源中添加一条通知，说明您\n我已经修改了它，并附上了日期和简要说明\n您已经修改了它。\n\n3.4您可以将承保来源或修改后的承保来源传达给\n与本许可证条款不同的许可证条款\n但条件是：\n\nA)您始终遵守第3.3款的规定；以及\n\nB)您向任何人提供本许可证的副本\n传达承保来源或修改后的承保来源。\n\n\n4制造和运输产品\n\n您可以制造产品和/或运输产品，前提是您必须确保\n产品的接收者有权访问任何适用的通知\n到产品。\n\n\n5免责声明和责任\n\n5.1担保免责声明--所涵盖的来源和任何产品\n按原样提供，且任何明示或默示保证，\n包括但不限于以下默示保证\n适销性，质量令人满意，不侵权\n第三方权利，以及对特定目的或用途的适用性\n就任何来源或产品向\n法律允许的最大范围。许可方未作出任何\n任何来源或产品不会或不会的声明\n侵犯任何专利、版权、商业秘密或其他\n所有权。关于使用、质量和\n任何来源或产品的性能应与您在一起，而不是\n许可方。本免责声明是必不可少的一部分\n以及授予任何权利的条件\n根据本牌照批给的。\n\n5.2责任的免除和限制--许可方应\n在法律允许的最大范围内，不对\n直接的，间接的，特殊的，偶然的，必然的，模范的，\n任何性质的惩罚性或其他损害赔偿，包括\n限制、替代货物或服务的采购、损失\n使用、数据或利润或业务中断\n以及任何关于合同、保证、侵权行为(包括\n疏忽)、产品责任或其他，以任何方式引起\n相对于覆盖的来源，修改的覆盖的来源\n和/或产品的制造或运输，即使被告知\n发生此类损害的可能性，您应持有\n许可方(S)不受任何责任、费用、\n损害赔偿、费用及开支，包括申索由第三方提供，\n与该等用途有关。\n\n\n6项专利\n\n6.1除本牌照的条款及条件另有规定外，\n许可方特此授予您永久的、全球范围的、\n非独家、免费、免版税、不可撤销(除\n在本第6条所述，或在许可方终止的情况下\n专利许可证制造、制造、使用、要约\n销售、销售、导入或以其他方式转让所涵盖的来源\n和产品，如果该许可仅适用于该专利\n可由该许可方许可的索赔必须\n因行使所涵盖来源项下的权利而受到侵犯\n由该许可方传达。\n\n6.2如果您对任何实体提起专利诉讼(包括\n诉讼中的交叉索赔或反索赔)声称\n承保来源或产品构成直接或贡献\n专利侵权，或者您寻求任何专利声明\n根据本许可证授予您的许可无效或不可强制执行\n则根据本许可证授予您的任何权利\n自启动此流程之日起终止。\n\n\n7总则\n\n7.1如果本许可证的任何规定是或其后成为\n无效或因任何原因无法强制执行，其余\n有关规定继续有效。\n\n7.2您不应使用任何名称(包括首字母缩写和\n缩写)、图像或标志，许可方或欧洲核子研究组织\n已知，除非需要遵守第3条，或\n在其他方面，法律允许这种使用。任何该等许可用途\n应为事实，不得使人联想到任何形式\n许可方的背书或暗示的参与，或\n它的人员。\n\n7.3欧洲核子研究中心可以发布本许可证的更新版本和变体\n它认为这符合本版本的精神，但可能\n在细节上有所不同，以解决新的问题或顾虑。新的\n将发布版本ED具有唯一的版本号和\n指定变量的变量标识符。如果许可方有\n指定给定的变体应用于所涵盖的源代码\n在不指定版本的情况下，您可以将所涵盖的源代码\n根据CERN-OHL的任何版本发布，\n变种。如果未指定变体，则所涵盖的来源应为\n被视为根据CERN-OHL-S释放。许可方可以\n还指定所涵盖的来源受特定的\nCERN-OHL的版本或任何更高版本，在这种情况下\n可应用此或任何更高版本的CERN-OHL\nCERN发布的变量标识符。\n\n7.4除许可方外，本许可证不得强制执行\n第三方受益人的权利是\n明确排除在外。', NULL);
INSERT INTO `license` VALUES (106, '2023-05-11 23:28:24', 'psutils', 'psutils License', 'https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/Licensing/psutils', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, '<<beginOptional>> PS Utilities Package<<endOptional>> <<var;name=\"copyright\";original=\"The constituent files of this package listed below are copyright (C) 1991-1995 Angus J. C. Duggan.\n\nLICENSE Makefile.msc Makefile.nt Makefile.os2\n\nMakefile.unix README config.h descrip.mms\n\nepsffit.c epsffit.man extractres.man extractres.pl\n\nfixdlsrps.man fixdlsrps.pl fixfmps.man fixfmps.pl\n\nfixmacps.man fixmacps.pl fixpsditps.man fixpsditps.pl\n\nfixpspps.man fixpspps.pl fixscribeps.man fixscribeps.pl\n\nfixtpps.man fixtpps.pl fixwfwps.man fixwfwps.pl\n\nfixwpps.man fixwpps.pl fixwwps.man fixwwps.pl\n\ngetafm getafm.man includeres.man includeres.pl\n\nmaketext patchlev.h psbook.c psbook.man\n\npserror.c pserror.h psmerge.man psmerge.pl\n\npsnup.c psnup.man psresize.c psresize.man\n\npsselect.c psselect.man psspec.c psspec.h\n\npstops.c pstops.man psutil.c psutil.h\n\nshowchar\";match=\".{0,1000}\">>\n\nThey may be copied and used for any purpose (including distribution as part of a for-profit product), provided:\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1)\";match=\".{0,20}\">> The original attribution of the programs is clearly displayed in the product and/or documentation, even if the programs are modified and/or renamed as part of the product.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"2)\";match=\".{0,20}\">> The original source code of the programs is provided free of charge (except for reasonable distribution costs). For a definition of reasonable distribution costs, see the Gnu General Public License or Larry Wall\'s Artistic License (provided with the Perl 4 kit). The GPL and Artistic License in NO WAY affect this license; they are merely used as examples of the spirit in which it is intended.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"3)\";match=\".{0,20}\">> These programs are provided \"as-is\". No warranty or guarantee of their fitness for any particular task is provided. Use of these programs is completely at your own risk.\n\nBasically, I don\'t mind how you use the programs so long as you acknowledge the author, and give people the originals if they want them.', 'PS Utilities Package\n\nThe constituent files of this package listed below are copyright (C) 1991-1995 Angus J. C. Duggan.\n\nLICENSE          Makefile.msc     Makefile.nt	   Makefile.os2\nMakefile.unix    README           config.h         descrip.mms\nepsffit.c        epsffit.man	  extractres.man   extractres.pl\nfixdlsrps.man    fixdlsrps.pl     fixfmps.man	   fixfmps.pl\nfixmacps.man     fixmacps.pl	  fixpsditps.man   fixpsditps.pl\nfixpspps.man     fixpspps.pl	  fixscribeps.man  fixscribeps.pl\nfixtpps.man	 fixtpps.pl	  fixwfwps.man     fixwfwps.pl\nfixwpps.man	 fixwpps.pl	  fixwwps.man	   fixwwps.pl\ngetafm           getafm.man	  includeres.man   includeres.pl\nmaketext         patchlev.h	  psbook.c         psbook.man\npserror.c        pserror.h        psmerge.man	   psmerge.pl\npsnup.c          psnup.man        psresize.c	   psresize.man\npsselect.c	 psselect.man     psspec.c         psspec.h\npstops.c         pstops.man	  psutil.c         psutil.h\nshowchar\n\nThey may be copied and used for any purpose (including distribution as part of a for-profit product), provided:\n\n1) The original attribution of the programs is clearly displayed in the product and/or documentation, even if the programs are modified and/or renamed as part of the product.\n\n2) The original source code of the programs is provided free of charge (except for reasonable distribution costs). For a definition of reasonable distribution costs, see the Gnu General Public License or Larry Wall\'s Artistic License (provided with the Perl 4 kit). The GPL and Artistic License in NO WAY affect this license; they are merely used as examples of the spirit in which it is intended.\n\n3) These programs are provided \"as-is\". No warranty or guarantee of their fitness for any particular task is provided. Use of these programs is completely at your own risk.\n\nBasically, I don\'t mind how you use the programs so long as you acknowledge the author, and give people the originals if they want them.', 'PS实用程序包\n\n下面列出的此程序包的组成文件是版权所有(C)1991-1995 Angus J.C.Duggan。\n\n许可证生成文件.msc生成文件.nt生成文件.os2\nMakefile.unix自述配置.h描述.mms\nEpsffit.c epsffit.man提取.man提取.pl\n修复lsrps.man修复lsrps.pl修复fmps.man修复fmps.pl\nFix macps.man fix macps.pl fix psditps.man fix psditps.pl\n修复pspps.man修复pspps.pl修复脚本pps.man修复脚本beps.pl\nFix tpps.man fix tpps.pl fix wfwps.man fix wfwps.pl\n修复wpps.man修复wpps.pl修复wwps.man修复wwps.pl\nGetafm getafm.man包括.man包括.pl\nMaketext patchlev.h psbook.c psbook.man\nPserror.c pserror.h psmerge.man psmerge.pl\nPsnup.c psnup.man Pssize.c Pssize.man\nPsselt.c Pselect.man Psspec.c Psspec.h\nPstops.c pstops.man psutil.c psutil.h\n放映时间\n\n它们可以被复制并用于任何目的(包括作为营利性产品的一部分进行分发)，前提是：\n\n1)即使程序作为产品的一部分进行了修改和/或重命名，程序的原始属性也会清楚地显示在产品和/或文档中。\n\n2)免费提供程序的原始源代码(除合理的分发费用外)。有关合理分发成本的定义，请参阅GNU通用公共许可证或Larry Wall的艺术许可证(随Perl4工具包提供)。GPL和艺术许可不以任何方式影响这一许可；它们只是被用作其意图的精神的例子。\n\n3)这些程序是按原样提供的。不提供他们是否适合任何特定任务的保证或保证。使用这些程序的风险完全由您自己承担。\n\n基本上，我不介意你如何使用这些程序，只要你承认作者，如果他们想要的话，把原件给他们。', NULL);
