 than the text found in the Original Code Source Code for Your Modifications.]\n\nEXHIBIT B.\n\n\"Part of the software embedded in this product is gSOAP software.\nPortions created by gSOAP are Copyright (C) 2001-2009 Robert A. van Engelen, Genivia inc. All Rights Reserved.\nTHE SOFTWARE IN THIS PRODUCT WAS IN PART PROVIDED BY GENIVIA INC AND ANY EXPRESS OR IMPLIED WARRANTIES, INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, THE IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY AND FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE ARE DISCLAIMED. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHOR BE LIABLE FOR ANY DIRECT, INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, EXEMPLARY, OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES (INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, PROCUREMENT OF SUBSTITUTE GOODS OR SERVICES; LOSS OF USE, DATA, OR PROFITS; OR BUSINESS INTERRUPTION) HOWEVER CAUSED AND ON ANY THEORY OF LIABILITY, WHETHER IN CONTRACT, STRICT LIABILITY, OR TORT (INCLUDING NEGLIGENCE OR OTHERWISE) ARISING IN ANY WAY OUT OF THE USE OF THIS SOFTWARE, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGE.\"', 'GSOAP公共许可证\n\n版本1.3b\n\nGSOAP公共许可证派生自Mozilla公共许可证(MPL1.1)。从最初的MPL1.1案文中删除的部分是1.0.1、2.1.(C)、(D)、2.2.(C)、(D)、8.2.(B)、10和11。增加了3.8节。修改后的部分为2.1(B)、2.2(B)、3.2(简化)、3.5(删除最后一句)和3.6(简化)。\n\n本许可证适用于gSOAP软件包，但位于gsoap/src和gsoap/wsdl中的soapcpp2和wsdl2.0源代码、由soapcpp2和wsdl2.h生成的所有代码、UDDI源代码gsoap/uddi2和Web服务器示例源代码Samples/Web服务器除外。要将这些软件工具和组件用于商业用途，需要商业许可证，可从www.genivia.com获得。\n\n1定义。\n\n1.0.1。\n1.1.“贡献者”是指创建或参与创建修改的每个实体。\n\n1.2.“贡献者版本”是指原始代码、贡献者使用的先前修改和该特定贡献者所做的修改的组合。\n\n1.3.“涵盖代码”是指原始代码或修改或原始代码和修改的组合，在每种情况下都包括其部分。\n\n1.4.“电子分发机制”是指软件开发界普遍接受的数据电子传输机制。\n\n1.5.“可执行代码”是指除源代码以外的任何形式的所涵盖代码。\n\n1.6.“初始开发者”是指附件A要求的源代码通知中确定为初始开发者的个人或实体。\n\n1.7.“较大的作品”是指将所涵盖的代码或其部分与不受本许可证条款管辖的代码相结合的作品。\n\n1.8.“许可证”指的是本文件。\n\n1.8.1。“可许可的”是指有权在最大可能的范围内，无论是在最初授予时还是在随后获得的时候，授予任何以及本协议所传达的所有权利。\n\n1.9.“修改”是指对原始规范或之前的任何修改的实质或结构进行的任何增加或删除。当所涵盖的代码以一系列文件的形式发布时，修改为：\nA.对包含原始代码或先前修改的文件的内容进行任何添加或删除。\nB.包含原始代码或先前修改的任何部分的任何新文件。\n\n1.10.“原始代码”是指在附件A所要求的源代码通知中描述为原始代码的计算机软件代码的源代码，并且在根据本许可证发布时，它还不是受本许可证管辖的代码。\n\n1.10.1.“专利权利要求”是指现在拥有或今后获得的任何专利权利要求(S)，包括但不限于，方法、过程和设备权利要求，任何可由授予人许可的专利权利要求。\n\n1.11.“源代码”是指所涵盖代码的首选形式，用于对其进行修改，包括其包含的所有模块，以及任何相关的接口定义文件、用于控制可执行文件的编译和安装的脚本，或与原始代码或贡献者选择的另一个众所周知的、可用的覆盖代码进行的源代码差异比较。源代码可以是压缩的或存档的形式，只要广泛免费提供适当的解压缩或解存档软件。\n\n1.12。“您”(或“您的”)是指根据本许可证或根据6.1节发布的本许可证的未来版本行使权利并遵守其所有条款的个人或法人实体。对于法人实体，“您”包括控制、受您控制或与您处于共同控制之下的任何实体。就本定义而言，“控制”是指：(A)直接或间接地通过合同或其他方式对这类实体进行指挥或管理的权力E、或(B)持有该实体50%以上的流通股或实益所有权。\n\n2源代码许可证。\n\n2.1.最初的开发者格兰特。\n初始开发商特此授予您全球范围的、免版税的非独家许可，受第三方知识产权声明的约束：\n(A)在知识产权(专利或商标除外)下，初始开发者可许可使用、复制、修改、展示、执行、再许可和分发原始代码(或其部分)，并修改或不修改，和/或作为较大作品的一部分；和\n(B)在初始开发者现在或以后拥有或控制的专利下，制作、制作、使用和销售(“出售和进口”)原始代码、修改或其部分，但仅限于为使您能够单独或与其他软件组合使用原始代码、修改或其任何组合或部分而合理必需的任何此类专利。\n(C)\n(D)\n\n2.2.贡献者格兰特。\n根据第三方知识产权声明，每个贡献者特此授予您全球范围的、免版税的、非独家许可\n(A)在可由贡献者许可的知识产权(专利或商标除外)下，在未经修改的基础上使用、复制、修改、展示、执行、再许可和分发由该贡献者创建的修改(或其部分)，连同其他修改、作为所涵盖的代码和/或作为更大作品的一部分；和\n(B)在贡献者现在或以后拥有或控制的专利下，制造、制造、使用和销售(“出售和进口”)贡献者版本(或其部分)，但仅限于使您能够单独或与其他软件组合使用贡献者版本(或其部分)所合理需要的任何此类专利。\n(C)\n(D)\n\n3.分配义务。\n\n3.1.应用许可证的问题。\n您创建或贡献的修改受本许可证条款的约束，包括但不限于第2.2条。所涵盖代码的源代码版本只能根据本许可证的条款或根据第6.1节发布的本许可证的未来版本进行分发，并且您必须将本许可证的副本包括在您分发的每个源代码副本中。您不得在任何源代码版本上提供或强加任何条款，以更改或限制本许可证的适用版本或接受者在本许可证下的权利。但是，您可以包括一份附加文档，提供第3.5节中所述的附加权利。\n\n3.2.源代码的可用性。\n您创建的任何修改都将以源代码形式提供给初始开发者，并受许可证条款的约束。\n\n3.3.修改说明。\n您必须使您贡献的所有涵盖代码包含一个文件，该文件记录了您为创建该涵盖代码所做的更改以及任何更改的日期。您必须包括一个突出的声明，说明修改直接或间接源自初始开发者提供的原始代码，并在(A)源代码和(B)可执行版本或相关文档中描述所涵盖代码的来源或所有权的任何声明中包含初始开发者的姓名。\n\n3.4.知识产权很重要。\n(A)第三方索赔。如果贡献者知道需要第三方知识产权下的许可证才能行使该贡献者根据第2.1或2.2节授予的权利，则贡献者必须包括一个标题为“Legal”的源代码分发的文本文件，该文件详细描述了索赔和提出索赔的一方，以便收件人知道联系谁。如果贡献者在按照第3.2节《贡献者》中所述提供修改后获得该等知识R应迅速修改贡献者此后提供的所有副本中的法律文件，并应采取合理的其他步骤(例如通知适当的邮件列表或新闻组)，以通知收到所涵盖代码的人已获得新的知识。\n\n(B)贡献者API。如果贡献者的修改包括应用程序编程接口，并且贡献者知道实施该API合理所需的专利许可，则贡献者还必须在法律文件中包含此信息。\n\n(C)申述。贡献者声明，除根据上述第3.4(A)节披露的情况外，贡献者认为贡献者的修改是贡献者的原创作品(S)和/或贡献者有足够的权利授予本许可证所传达的权利。\n\n3.5.所需的通知。\n您必须在源代码的每个文件中复制附件A中的通知。如果由于其结构原因，无法将此类通知放入特定源代码文件中，则您必须在用户可能会查找此类通知的位置(如相关目录)中包含此类通知。如果您创建了一项或多项修改(S)，您可以将您的姓名作为贡献者添加到附件A中描述的通知中。您还必须在描述接受者权利或与所涵盖代码相关的所有权的任何源代码文档中复制本许可证。您可以选择向所涵盖代码的一个或多个收件人提供保修、支持、赔偿或责任义务，并收取费用。但是，您只能代表您自己这样做，而不能代表最初的开发者或任何贡献者。\n\n3.6.可执行版本的分发。\n仅当所涵盖的代码满足第3.1-3.5节的要求时，您才能以可执行形式分发所涵盖的代码。您可以根据您选择的许可证分发所涵盖代码或所有权的可执行版本CE，它可能包含与本许可证不同的条款，前提是您遵守本许可证的条款，并且可执行版本的许可证不试图限制或更改接受者在源代码版本中的权利，而不是本许可证中规定的权利。如果您在不同的许可证下分发可执行版本，您必须绝对明确，任何与本许可证不同的条款都是由您单独提供的，而不是由初始开发者或任何贡献者提供。如果您将包含所涵盖代码的可执行版本作为产品的一部分分发，则必须在随产品提供的文档和/或其他材料中复制附件B中的声明。\n\n3.7.更大的作品。\n您可以通过将所涵盖的代码与不受本许可证条款管辖的其他代码相结合来创建较大的作品，并将较大的作品作为单个产品分发。在这种情况下，您必须确保所涵盖代码满足本许可证的要求。\n\n3.8.限制。\n您不能从gSOAP中删除任何产品标识、版权、专有声明或标签。\n\n4因法规或规章而不能遵守的。\n\n如果由于法规、司法命令或法规的原因，您无法就所涵盖的部分或全部代码遵守本许可证的任何条款，则您必须：(A)最大限度地遵守本许可证的条款；以及(B)描述限制及其影响的代码。此类描述必须包含在3.4节中描述的法律文件中，并且必须包含在源代码的所有分发版本中。除法规或条例禁止的范围外，此类描述必须足够详细，使普通技术人员能够理解。\n\n5本许可证的适用范围。\n\n本许可证适用于初始开发者附加了附件A中的通知的代码以及相关的涵盖代码。\n\n许可证的6个版本。\n\n6.1.新版本。\n设保人可不时发布本许可证的修订版本和/或新版本。每个版本都会有一个不同的版本号。\n\n6.2.新版本的效果。\n所涵盖的代码在许可证的特定版本下发布后，您可以始终根据该版本的条款继续使用它。您也可以根据许可证的任何后续版本的条款选择使用此类所涵盖的代码。\n\n6.3.衍生作品。\n如果您创建或使用本许可证的修改版本(您这样做可能只是为了将其应用于不受本许可证管辖的代码)，您必须(A)重命名您的许可证，使短语“gSOAP”或任何令人困惑的相似短语不会出现在您的许可证中(注意您的许可证与本许可证不同)和(B)以其他方式明确您的许可证版本包含不同于gSOAP公共许可证的条款。(在附件A中描述的通知中填写初始开发者、原始代码或贡献者的名称本身不应被视为对本许可证的修改。)\n\n7免责声明。\n\n在本许可证下，所涵盖的代码按原样提供，不提供任何明示、默示或法定的担保，包括但不限于适销性、适用性、不侵犯第三方知识产权的默示担保，以及因交易习惯、习惯或交易过程而产生的任何担保。在不限制上述规定的情况下，您承认本软件是按原样提供的，并且作者不保证本软件将不间断运行或无错误。有限责任软件的结果和性能的全部风险由您承担。在任何情况下，作者都不对任何种类或性质的特殊、间接、附带、惩罚性或后果性损害负责，无论是基于CONTRACT、保修、侵权(包括疏忽)、严格责任或其他以任何方式与软件有关的责任，即使作者已被告知此类损害的可能性，或者此类损害是可以合理预见的，并且即使所提供的任何排他性补救措施的基本目的失败了。此类损害赔偿限制包括但不限于商誉损失、利润损失、数据或软件丢失、工作中断、计算机故障或其他商品的故障或减损的损害赔偿。在任何情况下，作者均不承担购买替代软件或服务的费用。您承认本软件不适用于危险环境中的在线设备，如核设施操作、飞机导航或控制或生命关键应用程序。作者明确表示不承担因在危险环境中的任何此类在线设备中使用本软件而产生的任何责任，也不接受因您在危险环境中的任何此类在线设备中使用本软件而导致的任何行为或索赔的任何责任。就本款而言，术语“生命关键应用程序”是指软件的运行或故障可能直接或间接导致人身伤害或生命损失的应用程序。本免责声明是本许可证的重要组成部分。除本免责声明外，不得在本协议下授权使用任何所涵盖的代码。\n\n8终止。\n\n8.1.如果您未能遵守本许可证中的条款，并且未能在意识到违规行为后30天内纠正此类违规行为，则本许可证及其授予的权利将自动终止。适当授予的对所涵盖代码的所有从属许可在本许可证的任何终止后仍然有效。根据其性质，在本许可证终止后必须保持有效的条款将继续有效。\n\n8.2.\n\n8.3.如果你这个笨蛋ERT针对参与者的专利侵权索赔，声称该参与者的贡献者版本直接或间接侵犯了任何专利。如果此类索赔在发起专利侵权诉讼之前得到解决(例如通过许可或和解)，则在确定任何付款或许可的金额或价值时，应考虑该参与者根据第2.1或2.2条授予的许可的合理价值。\n\n8.4.如果根据上述条款8.1或8.2终止，您或任何分销商在终止前在本协议项下有效授予的所有最终用户许可协议(不包括分销商和经销商)在终止后仍然有效。\n\n9责任限制。\n\n在任何情况下，根据任何法律理论，无论侵权(包括疏忽)、合同或其他，您、初始开发者、任何其他贡献者、所涵盖代码的任何分发者或任何此等各方的任何供应商，都不对任何人承担任何间接、特殊、附带或后果性的损害，包括但不限于商誉损失、停工、计算机故障或故障的损害，或任何和所有其他商业损害或损失，即使此方已被告知此类损害的可能性。在适用法律禁止的范围内，这一责任限制不适用于该当事人的疏忽造成的死亡或人身伤害的责任。某些司法管辖区不允许排除或限制附带或后果性损害，因此此排除和限制可能不适用于您。\n\n10个美国政府最终用户。\n\n11其他。\n\n12索赔责任。\n\n在初始开发者和贡献者之间，各方对因使用本许可证下的权利而直接或间接产生的索赔和损害负责，并且您同意与初始开发者和贡献者合作。在公平的基础上分配这种责任。本协议没有任何意图，也不应被视为构成任何责任的承认。\n\n证据A。\n\n“此文件的内容受gSOAP公共许可证版本1.3(”许可证“)的约束；除非遵守许可证，否则您不能使用此文件。您可以在以下位置获取许可证的副本\nHttp://www.cs.fsu.edu/Engelen/soaplicense.html\n根据本许可证分发的软件是按原样分发的，不提供任何明示或默示的担保。有关许可证下管理权利和限制的特定语言，请参阅许可证。\nGSOAP软件的原始代码是：stdsoap.h、stdsoap2.h、stdsoap.c、stdsoap2.c、stdsoap.cpp、stdsoap2.cpp、soapcpp2.h、soapcpp2.c、soapcpp2_lex.l、soapcpp2_yacc.y、error2.h、error2.c、symb2.c、init2.c、soapdoc2.html、soapdoc2.pdf、httpget.h、stl.h、stldeque.h、stllist.h、stlvetor.h、stlset.h。\n原始代码的最初开发者是Robert A.van Engelen。Robert A.van Engelen创建的部分版权所有(C)2001-2004 Robert A.van Engelen，Genivia Inc.保留所有权利。\n撰稿(S)：\n“_\n[注：本附件A的文本可能与原始代码的源代码文件中的通知文本略有不同。您应使用本附件A的文本进行修改，而不是使用原始代码源代码中的文本。]\n\n证据B。\n\n这款产品中嵌入的部分软件是gSoap软件。\n由gSOAP创建的部分版权所有(C)2001-2009 Robert A.van Engelen，Genivia Inc.保留所有权利。\n本产品中的软件部分由GENIVIA Inc.提供，任何明示或默示担保，包括但不限于对适销性和特定用途适用性的默示担保，均予以否认。在任何情况下，作者不对任何直接、间接、附带、特殊、惩罚性或后果性损害(包括但不限于采购替代产品或服务；损失使用、数据或利润；或业务中断)，但根据任何责任理论，无论是合同责任、严格责任或因使用本软件而以任何方式产生的侵权(包括疏忽或其他)，即使被告知此类损害的可能性也是如此。', NULL);
INSERT INTO `license` VALUES (160, '2023-05-11 23:28:24', 'VSL-1.0', 'Vovida Software License v1.0', 'https://opensource.org/licenses/VSL-1.0', 0, 0, 1, 0, NULL, '<<beginOptional>> Vovida Software License v. 1.0<<endOptional>><<beginOptional>> This license applies to all software incorporated in the \"Vovida Open Communication Application Library\" except for those portions incorporating third party software specifically identified as being licensed under separate license.<<endOptional>><<beginOptional>> The Vovida Software License, Version 1.0<<endOptional>> <<var;name=\"copyright\";original=\"Copyright (c) 2000 Vovida Networks, Inc. All rights reserved.\";match=\".{0,1000}\">>\n\nRedistribution and use in source and binary forms, with or without modification, are permitted provided that the following conditions are met:\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Redistributions of source code must retain the above copyright notice, this list of conditions and the following disclaimer.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"2.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Redistributions in binary form must reproduce the above copyright notice, this list of conditions and the following disclaimer in the documentation and/or other materials provided with the distribution.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"3.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> The names \"VOCAL\", \"Vovida Open Communication Application Library\", and \"Vovida Open Communication Application Library (VOCAL)\" must not be used to endorse or promote products derived from this software without prior written permission. For written permission, please contact vocal@vovida.org.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"4.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Products derived from this software may not be called \"VOCAL\", nor may \"VOCAL\" appear in their name, without prior written permission.\n\nTHIS SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\" AND ANY EXPRESSED OR IMPLIED WARRANTIES, INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, THE IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, TITLE AND NON-INFRINGEMENT ARE DISCLAIMED. IN NO EVENT SHALL VOVIDA NETWORKS, INC. OR ITS CONTRIBUTORS BE LIABLE FOR ANY DAMAGES IN EXCESS OF $1,000, NOR FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, EXEMPLARY, OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES (INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, PROCUREMENT OF SUBSTITUTE GOODS OR SERVICES; LOSS OF USE, DATA, OR PROFITS; OR BUSINESS INTERRUPTION) HOWEVER CAUSED AND ON ANY THEORY OF LIABILITY, WHETHER IN CONTRACT, STRICT LIABILITY, OR TORT (INCLUDING NEGLIGENCE OR OTHERWISE) ARISING IN ANY WAY OUT OF THE USE OF THIS SOFTWARE, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGE.', 'Vovida Software License v. 1.0\n\nThis license applies to all software incorporated in the \"Vovida Open Communication Application Library\" except for those portions incorporating third party software specifically identified as being licensed under separate license.\n\nThe Vovida Software License, Version 1.0\nCopyright (c) 2000 Vovida Networks, Inc. All rights reserved.\n\nRedistribution and use in source and binary forms, with or without modification, are permitted provided that the following conditions are met:\n\n1. Redistributions of source code must retain the above copyright notice, this list of conditions and the following disclaimer.\n\n2. Redistributions in binary form must reproduce the above copyright notice, this list of conditions and the following disclaimer in the documentation and/or other materials provided with the distribution.\n\n3. The names \"VOCAL\", \"Vovida Open Communication Application Library\", and \"Vovida Open Communication Application Library (VOCAL)\" must not be used to endorse or promote products derived from this software without prior written permission. For written permission, please contact vocal@vovida.org.\n\n4. Products derived from this software may not be called \"VOCAL\", nor may \"VOCAL\" appear in their name, without prior written permission.\n\nTHIS SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\" AND ANY EXPRESSED OR IMPLIED WARRANTIES, INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, THE IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, TITLE AND NON-INFRINGEMENT ARE DISCLAIMED. IN NO EVENT SHALL VOVIDA NETWORKS, INC. OR ITS CONTRIBUTORS BE LIABLE FOR ANY DAMAGES IN EXCESS OF $1,000, NOR FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, EXEMPLARY, OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES (INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, PROCUREMENT OF SUBSTITUTE GOODS OR SERVICES; LOSS OF USE, DATA, OR PROFITS; OR BUSINESS INTERRUPTION) HOWEVER CAUSED AND ON ANY THEORY OF LIABILITY, WHETHER IN CONTRACT, STRICT LIABILITY, OR TORT (INCLUDING NEGLIGENCE OR OTHERWISE) ARISING IN ANY WAY OUT OF THE USE OF THIS SOFTWARE, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGE.', 'Vovida软件许可证v1.0\n\n本许可证适用于“Vovida开放式通信应用程序库”中包含的所有软件，但包含第三方软件的部分除外，这些第三方软件被明确指定为在单独许可证下获得许可。\n\nVovida软件许可证，版本1.0\n版权所有(C)2000 Vovida Networks，Inc.保留所有权利。\n\n在满足以下条件的情况下，允许以源代码和二进制形式重新分发和使用，无论是否进行修改：\n\n1.源代码的再分发必须保留上述版权声明、此条件列表和以下免责声明。\n\n2.二进制形式的再分发必须在随分发提供的文档和/或其他材料中复制上述版权声明、此条件列表和以下免责声明。\n\n3.未经事先书面许可，不得使用“Voice”、“Vovida Open Communication Application Library”和“Vovida Open Communication Application Library(Voice)”等名称为本软件衍生的产品代言或促销。如需书面许可，请联系vocal@vovida.org。\n\n4.未经事先书面许可，从本软件衍生的产品不得被称为“VOICAL”，也不得在其名称中出现“VOICE”。\n\n本软件按原样提供，任何明示或默示的保证，包括但不限于对适销性、特定用途的适用性、所有权和不侵权的默示保证，均予以否认。在任何情况下，VOVIDA Networks，Inc.或其贡献者对超过1,000美元的任何损害承担责任，也不对因使用T而引起的任何间接、附带、特殊、惩罚性或后果性损害(包括但不限于购买替代商品或服务；失去使用、数据或利润；或业务中断)以及任何责任理论，无论是合同责任、严格责任或侵权(包括疏忽或其他)负责他的软件，即使被告知有这种损坏的可能性。', NULL);
INSERT INTO `license` VALUES (161, '2023-05-11 23:28:23', 'FTL', 'Freetype Project License', 'http://freetype.fis.uniroma2.it/FTL.TXT,http://git.savannah.gnu.org/cgit/freetype/freetype2.git/tree/docs/FTL.TXT', 0, 0, 0, 1, NULL, '<<beginOptional>> The FreeType Project LICENSE\n\n2006-Jan-27<<endOptional>><<beginOptional>> Copyright 1996-2002, 2006 by David Turner, Robert Wilhelm, and Werner Lemberg\n\nIntroduction\n\nThe FreeType Project is distributed in several archive packages; some of them may contain, in addition to the FreeType font engine, various tools and contributions which rely on, or relate to, the FreeType Project.\n\nThis license applies to all files found in such packages, and which do not fall under their own explicit license. The license affects thus the FreeType font engine, the test programs, documentation and makefiles, at the very least.\n\nThis license was inspired by the BSD, Artistic, and IJG (Independent JPEG Group) licenses, which all encourage inclusion and use of free software in commercial and freeware products alike. As a consequence, its main points are that:\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"o\";match=\".{0,20}\">> We don\'t promise that this software works. However, we will be interested in any kind of bug reports. (`as is\' distribution)\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"o\";match=\".{0,20}\">> You can use this software for whatever you want, in parts or full form, without having to pay us. (`royalty-free\' usage)\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"o\";match=\".{0,20}\">> You may not pretend that you wrote this software. If you use it, or only parts of it, in a program, you must acknowledge somewhere in your documentation that you have used the FreeType code. (`credits\')\n\nWe specifically permit and encourage the inclusion of this software, with or without modifications, in commercial products. We disclaim all warranties covering The FreeType Project and assume no liability related to The FreeType Project.\n\nFinally, many people asked us for a preferred form for a credit/disclaimer to use in compliance with this license. We thus encourage you to use the following text:\n\n\"\"\" Portions of this software are copyright © <year> The FreeType Project (www.freetype.org). All rights reserved. \"\"\"\n\nPlease replace <year> with the value from the FreeType version you actually use.<<endOptional>>\n\nLegal Terms\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"0.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Definitions\n\n   Throughout this license, the terms `package\', `FreeType Project\', and `FreeType archive\' refer to the set of files originally distributed by the authors (David Turner, Robert Wilhelm, and Werner Lemberg) as the `FreeType Project\', be they named as alpha, beta or final release.\n\n   `You\' refers to the licensee, or person using the project, where `using\' is a generic term including compiling the project\'s source code as well as linking it to form a `program\' or `executable\'. This program is referred to as `a program using the FreeType engine\'.\n\n   This license applies to all files distributed in the original FreeType Project, including all source code, binaries and documentation, unless otherwise stated in the file in its original, unmodified form as distributed in the original archive. If you are unsure whether or not a particular file is covered by this license, you must contact us to verify this.\n\n   The FreeType Project is copyright (C) 1996-2000 by David Turner, Robert Wilhelm, and Werner Lemberg. All rights reserved except as specified below.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> No Warranty\n\n   THE FREETYPE PROJECT IS PROVIDED `AS IS\' WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EITHER EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY AND FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. IN NO EVENT WILL ANY OF THE AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY DAMAGES CAUSED BY THE USE OR THE INABILITY TO USE, OF THE FREETYPE PROJECT.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"2.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Redistribution\n\n   This license grants a worldwide, royalty-free, perpetual and irrevocable right and license to use, execute, perform, compile, display, copy, create derivative works of, distribute and sublicense the FreeType Project (in both source and object code forms) and derivative works thereof for any purpose; and to authorize others to exercise some or all of the rights granted herein, subject to the following conditions:\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"o\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Redistribution of source code must retain this license file (`FTL.TXT\') unaltered; any additions, deletions or changes to the original files must be clearly indicated in accompanying documentation. The copyright notices of the unaltered, original files must be preserved in all copies of source files.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"o\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Redistribution in binary form must provide a disclaimer that states that the software is based in part of the work of the FreeType Team, in the distribution documentation. We also encourage you to put an URL to the FreeType web page in your documentation, though this isn\'t mandatory.\n\n   These conditions apply to any software derived from or based on the FreeType Project, not just the unmodified files. If you use our work, you must acknowledge us. However, no fee need be paid to us.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"3.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Advertising\n\n   Neither the FreeType authors and contributors nor you shall use the name of the other for commercial, advertising, or promotional purposes without specific prior written permission.\n\n   We suggest, but do not require, that you use one or more of the following phrases to refer to this software in your documentation or advertising materials: `FreeType Project\', `FreeType Engine\', `FreeType library\', or `FreeType Distribution\'.\n\n   As you have not signed this license, you are not required to accept it. However, as the FreeType Project is copyrighted material, only this license, or another one contracted with the authors, grants you the right to use, distribute, and modify it. Therefore, by using, distributing, or modifying the FreeType Project, you indicate that you understand and accept all the terms of this license.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"4.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Contacts\n\n   There are two mailing lists related to FreeType:\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"o\";match=\".{0,20}\">> freetype@nongnu.org\n\n      Discusses general use and applications of FreeType, as well as future and wanted additions to the library and distribution. If you are looking for support, start in this list if you haven\'t found anything to help you in the documentation.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"o\";match=\".{0,20}\">> freetype-devel@nongnu.org\n\n      Discusses bugs, as well as engine internals, design issues, specific licenses, porting, etc.\n\n   Our home page can be found at\n\n   http://www.freetype.org<<beginOptional>> --- end of FTL.TXT ---<<endOptional>>', 'The FreeType Project LICENSE\n\n2006-Jan-27\n\nCopyright 1996-2002, 2006 by David Turner, Robert Wilhelm, and Werner Lemberg\n\nIntroduction\n\nThe FreeType Project is distributed in several archive packages; some of them may contain, in addition to the FreeType font engine, various tools and contributions which rely on, or relate to, the FreeType Project.\n\nThis license applies to all files found in such packages, and which do not fall under their own explicit license. The license affects thus the FreeType font engine, the test programs, documentation and makefiles, at the very least.\n\nThis license was inspired by the BSD, Artistic, and IJG (Independent JPEG Group) licenses, which all encourage inclusion and use of free software in commercial and freeware products alike. As a consequence, its main points are that:\n\n     o We don\'t promise that this software works. However, we will be interested in any kind of bug reports. (`as is\' distribution)\n\n     o You can use this software for whatever you want, in parts or full form, without having to pay us. (`royalty-free\' usage)\n\n     o You may not pretend that you wrote this software. If you use it, or only parts of it, in a program, you must acknowledge somewhere in your documentation that you have used the FreeType code. (`credits\')\n\nWe specifically permit and encourage the inclusion of this software, with or without modifications, in commercial products. We disclaim all warranties covering The FreeType Project and assume no liability related to The FreeType Project.\n\nFinally, many people asked us for a preferred form for a credit/disclaimer to use in compliance with this license. We thus encourage you to use the following text:\n\n     \"\"\" Portions of this software are copyright © <year> The FreeType Project (www.freetype.org). All rights reserved. \"\"\"\n\nPlease replace <year> with the value from the FreeType version you actually use.\n\nLegal Terms\n\n0. Definitions\n\nThroughout this license, the terms `package\', `FreeType Project\', and `FreeType archive\' refer to the set of files originally distributed by the authors (David Turner, Robert Wilhelm, and Werner Lemberg) as the `FreeType Project\', be they named as alpha, beta or final release.\n\n`You\' refers to the licensee, or person using the project, where `using\' is a generic term including compiling the project\'s source code as well as linking it to form a `program\' or `executable\'. This program is referred to as `a program using the FreeType engine\'.\n\nThis license applies to all files distributed in the original FreeType Project, including all source code, binaries and documentation, unless otherwise stated in the file in its original, unmodified form as distributed in the original archive. If you are unsure whether or not a particular file is covered by this license, you must contact us to verify this.\n\nThe FreeType Project is copyright (C) 1996-2000 by David Turner, Robert Wilhelm, and Werner Lemberg. All rights reserved except as specified below.\n\n1. No Warranty\n\nTHE FREETYPE PROJECT IS PROVIDED `AS IS\' WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EITHER EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY AND FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. IN NO EVENT WILL ANY OF THE AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY DAMAGES CAUSED BY THE USE OR THE INABILITY TO USE, OF THE FREETYPE PROJECT.\n\n2. Redistribution\n\nThis license grants a worldwide, royalty-free, perpetual and irrevocable right and license to use, execute, perform, compile, display, copy, create derivative works of, distribute and sublicense the FreeType Project (in both source and object code forms) and derivative works thereof for any purpose; and to authorize others to exercise some or all of the rights granted herein, subject to the following conditions:\n\n     o Redistribution of source code must retain this license file (`FTL.TXT\') unaltered; any additions, deletions or changes to the original files must be clearly indicated in accompanying documentation. The copyright notices of the unaltered, original files must be preserved in all copies of source files.\n\n     o Redistribution in binary form must provide a disclaimer that states that the software is based in part of the work of the FreeType Team, in the distribution documentation. We also encourage you to put an URL to the FreeType web page in your documentation, though this isn\'t mandatory.\n\nThese conditions apply to any software derived from or based on the FreeType Project, not just the unmodified files. If you use our work, you must acknowledge us. However, no fee need be paid to us.\n\n3. Advertising\n\nNeither the FreeType authors and contributors nor you shall use the name of the other for commercial, advertising, or promotional purposes without specific prior written permission.\n\nWe suggest, but do not require, that you use one or more of the following phrases to refer to this software in your documentation or advertising materials: `FreeType Project\', `FreeType Engine\', `FreeType library\', or `FreeType Distribution\'.\n\nAs you have not signed this license, you are not required to accept it. However, as the FreeType Project is copyrighted material, only this license, or another one contracted with the authors, grants you the right to use, distribute, and modify it. Therefore, by using, distributing, or modifying the FreeType Project, you indicate that you understand and accept all the terms of this license.\n\n4. Contacts\n\nThere are two mailing lists related to FreeType:\n\n     o freetype@nongnu.org\n\n     Discusses general use and applications of FreeType, as well as future and wanted additions to the library and distribution. If you are looking for support, start in this list if you haven\'t found anything to help you in the documentation.\n\n     o freetype-devel@nongnu.org\n\n     Discusses bugs, as well as engine internals, design issues, specific licenses, porting, etc.\n\nOur home page can be found at\n\n http://www.freetype.org\n\n--- end of FTL.TXT ---', '自由类型项目许可证\n\n2006-1-27\n\n版权所有1996-2002，作者：David Turner、Robert Wilhelm和Werner Lemberg\n\n引言\n\nFreeType Project发布在几个存档包中；其中一些可能包含各种工具和贡献包，除了FreeType字体引擎之外，这些工具和贡献包依赖于或与FreeType Project相关。\n\n本许可证适用于此类包中的所有文件，并且不属于它们自己的显式许可证。因此，许可证至少会影响FreeType字体引擎、测试程序、文档和Make文件。\n\n该许可证的灵感来自BSD、ARTICAL和IJG(独立JPEG组)许可证，这些许可证都鼓励在商业和免费软件产品中包含和使用自由软件。因此，它的主要观点是：\n\nO我们不保证这个软件能正常工作。然而，我们会对任何类型的错误报告感兴趣。(“按原样”分配)\n\nO您可以将此软件用于您想要的任何内容，部分或全部，而无需向我们支付费用。(`免版税‘用法)\n\nO您不得假装是您编写了本软件。如果您在程序中使用它，或者只使用它的一部分，您必须在文档中的某个地方确认您已经使用了FreeType代码。(`信用‘)\n\n我们特别允许并鼓励将此软件包含在商业产品中，无论是否经过修改。我们不承担任何有关自由型项目的担保，也不承担任何与自由型项目相关的责任。\n\n最后，许多人要求我们提供符合本许可证的信用/免责声明的首选格式。因此，我们鼓励您使用以下案文：\n\n“本软件的某些部分是自由类型项目(www.freetype.org)的版权所有。保留所有权利。”©\n\n请用您实际使用的FreeType版本中的值替换<Year>。\n\n法律术语\n\n0。定义\n\n在本许可证中，术语`Package‘、`FreeType Project’、D‘FreeType存档’指的是最初由作者(David Turner、Robert Wilhelm和Werner Lemberg)分发的一组文件，称为‘Free Type Project’，无论它们被命名为Alpha、Beta或最终版本。\n\n“你”是指被许可人或使用该项目的人，其中“使用”是一个通用术语，包括编译该项目的源代码以及将其链接形成一个“程序”或“可执行文件”。这个程序被称为‘使用自由类型引擎的程序’。\n\n本许可证适用于原始FreeType Project中分发的所有文件，包括所有源代码、二进制文件和文档，除非文件中另有说明，该文件以原始档案中分发的原始、未经修改的形式发布。如果您不确定特定文件是否包含在本许可证中，您必须联系我们进行验证。\n\n自由类型项目版权所有(C)1996-2000，作者为David Turner、Robert Wilhelm和Werner Lemberg。除以下规定外，保留所有权利。\n\n1.没有保修\n\nFREETYPE项目按原样提供，不提供任何明示或默示的担保，包括但不限于对适销性和特定用途适用性的担保。在任何情况下，任何作者或版权所有者都不对因使用或无法使用FREETYPE项目而造成的任何损害承担任何责任。\n\n2.再分配\n\n本许可证授予全球范围内的、免版税、永久和不可撤销的权利和许可，以使用、执行、执行、编译、显示、复制、创建、分发和再许可用于任何目的的FreeType项目及其衍生作品(源代码和目标代码形式)及其衍生作品；并授权他人行使本文授予的部分或全部权利，但须满足以下条件：\n\nO源代码的再分发必须保持本许可证文件(`FTL.TXT‘)不变；对原始文件的任何添加、删除或更改都必须在附带的文档中明确注明。警察请注意，未更改的原始文件必须保存在源文件的所有副本中。\n\nO二进制形式的重新分发必须在分发文档中提供免责声明，声明软件是基于FreeType团队的部分工作。我们还鼓励您在文档中添加指向FreeType网页的URL，尽管这不是强制性的。\n\n这些条件适用于派生自或基于FreeType项目的任何软件，而不仅仅是未经修改的文件。如果你使用我们的作品，你必须承认我们。然而，不需要向我们支付任何费用。\n\n3.广告\n\n未经事先明确的书面许可，FreeType作者和贡献者以及您不得将他人的名称用于商业、广告或促销目的。\n\n我们建议(但不要求)您在文档或广告材料中使用以下一个或多个短语来指代本软件：`自由类型项目‘、`自由类型引擎’、‘自由类型库’或‘自由类型分发’。\n\n由于您尚未签署本许可证，因此您不需要接受它。然而，由于自由类型项目是受版权保护的材料，只有本许可证或与作者签订的另一份许可证授予您使用、分发和修改它的权利。因此，通过使用、分发或修改FreeType项目，即表示您理解并接受本许可证的所有条款。\n\n4.联系人\n\n有两个与FreeType相关的邮件列表：\n\n邮箱：freetype@nongnu.org\n\n讨论了FreeType的一般用法和应用，以及库和发行版的未来和需要添加的内容。如果您正在寻找支持，如果在文档中没有找到任何对您有帮助的内容，请从这个列表开始。\n\nO freetype-devel@nongnu.org\n\n讨论错误，以及引擎内部结构、设计问题、特定许可证、移植等。\n\n我们的主页可在\n\nHttp://www.freetype.org\n\n-FTL.TXT结束', 'This license was released 27 Jan 2006');
