 distributed on an \"AS IS\" basis, WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, either express or implied. See the License for the specific language governing rights and limitations under the License.\n\nThe Original Code is ______________________________________.\n\nThe Initial Developer of the Original Code is ________________________.\nPortions created by ______________________ are Copyright (C) ______\n_______________________. All Rights Reserved.\n\nContributor(s): ______________________________________.\n\nAlternatively, the contents of this file may be used under the terms of the _____ license (the  \"[___] License\"), in which case the provisions of [______] License are applicable instead of those above. If you wish to allow use of your version of this file only under the terms of the [____] License and not to allow others to use your version of this file under the MPL, indicate your decision by deleting the provisions above and replace them with the notice and other provisions required by the [___] License. If you do not delete the provisions above, a recipient may use your version of this file under either the MPL or the [___] License.\"\n\nNOTE: The text of this Exhibit A may differ slightly from the text of the notices in the Source Code files of the Original Code. You should use the text of this Exhibit A rather than the text found in the Original Code Source Code for Your Modifications.', 'Mozilla公共许可证版本1.1\n\n1.定义。\n\n1.0.1。“商业使用”是指将所涵盖的代码分发或以其他方式向第三方提供。\n\n1.1.“贡献者”是指创建或参与创建修改的每个实体。\n\n1.2.“贡献者版本”是指原始代码、贡献者使用的先前修改和该特定贡献者所做的修改的组合。\n\n1.3.“所涵盖的代码”是指原始代码或修改或原始代码和修改的组合，在每种情况下都包括其部分。\n\n1.4.“电子分发机制”是指软件开发界普遍接受的数据电子传输机制。\n\n1.5.“可执行代码”是指除源代码以外的任何形式的所涵盖代码。\n\n1.6.“初始开发者”是指附件A要求的源代码通知中确定为初始开发者的个人或实体。\n\n1.7.“较大的作品”是指将所涵盖的代码或其部分与不受本许可证条款管辖的代码相结合的作品。\n\n1.8.“许可证”指的是本文件。\n\n1.8.1。“可许可的”是指有权在最大可能的范围内，无论是在初始授予时还是在随后获得的时候，授予本协议所传达的任何和所有权利。\n\n1.9.“修改”是指对原始规范或之前的任何修改的实质或结构进行的任何增加或删除。当所涵盖的代码以一系列文件的形式发布时，修改为：\n对包含原始代码或先前修改的文件内容的任何添加或删除。\n包含原始代码或先前修改的任何部分的任何新文件。\n\n1.10.“原始代码”是指在附件A要求的源代码通知中描述为原始代码的计算机软件代码的源代码，并且在其发布时，根据本许可证不属于本许可证管辖的代码。\n\n1.10.1.“专利权利要求”是指现在拥有或今后获得的任何专利权利要求(S)，包括但不限于，方法、过程和设备权利要求，任何可由授予人许可的专利权利要求。\n\n1.11.“源代码”是指所涵盖代码的首选形式，用于对其进行修改，包括其包含的所有模块，以及任何相关的接口定义文件、用于控制可执行文件的编译和安装的脚本，或与原始代码或贡献者选择的另一个众所周知的、可用的覆盖代码进行的源代码差异比较。源代码可以是压缩的或存档的形式，只要广泛免费提供适当的解压缩或解存档软件。\n\n1.12。“您”(或“您的”)是指根据本许可证或根据6.1节发布的本许可证的未来版本行使权利并遵守其所有条款的个人或法人实体。对于法人实体，“您”包括控制、受您控制或与您处于共同控制之下的任何实体。在本定义中，“控制”是指(A)直接或间接地通过合同或其他方式引导或管理该实体的权力，或(B)拥有该实体50%(50%)以上的流通股或实益所有权。\n\n2.源代码许可证。\n\n2.1.最初的开发者格兰特。初始开发商特此授予您全球范围的、免版税的非独家许可，受第三方知识产权声明的约束：\n\nA.在知识产权(专利或商标除外)下，初始开发者可许可使用、复制、修改、展示、执行、再许可和分发原始代码(或其部分)，进行或不进行修改，和/或作为较大作品的一部分；以及\nB.根据制造侵犯的专利权利要求，美国NG或出售原始代码，制作、制造、使用、实践、出售和要约出售，和/或以其他方式处置原始代码(或其部分)。\nC.第2.1(A)和(B)节中授予的许可证自初始开发者根据本许可证条款首次分发原始代码之日起生效。\nD.尽管有上述第2.1(B)条的规定，以下情况不授予专利许可：1)从原始代码中删除的代码；2)与原始代码分开的代码；或3)由于以下原因造成的侵权行为：i)修改原始代码或ii)原始代码与其他软件或设备的组合。\n\n2.2.贡献者格兰特。根据第三方知识产权声明，每个贡献者特此授予您全球范围的、免版税的、非独家许可\n\nA.根据可由贡献者许可的知识产权(专利或商标除外)，在未经修改的基础上使用、复制、修改、显示、执行、再许可和分发由该贡献者创建的修改(或其部分)，作为所涵盖的代码和/或作为更大作品的一部分；和\nB.根据因制作、使用或销售由该贡献人单独和/或结合其贡献人版本(或该组合的一部分)所作的修改而侵犯的专利权利要求，以制作、使用、出售、要约出售、已作出和/或以其他方式处置：1)该贡献人所作的修改(或其部分)；以及2)该贡献人所作的修改与其贡献人版本(或该组合的一部分)的组合。\nC.第2.2(A)节和第2.2(B)节中授予的许可自贡献者首次将所涵盖代码用于商业用途之日起生效。\nD.尽管有上述第2.2(B)条的规定，但不授予任何专利许可：1)对于贡献者已从贡献者版本中删除的任何代码；2)与E贡献者版本；3)因以下原因造成的侵权行为：i)贡献者版本的第三方修改，或ii)该贡献者所做的修改与其他软件(贡献者版本的一部分除外)或其他设备的组合；或4)在该贡献者未进行修改的情况下，根据所涵盖代码侵犯的专利索赔。\n\n3.分配义务。\n\n3.1.许可证的申请。您创建或贡献的修改受本许可证条款的约束，包括但不限于第2.2条。所涵盖代码的源代码版本只能根据本许可证的条款或根据第6.1节发布的本许可证的未来版本进行分发，并且您必须将本许可证的副本包括在您分发的每个源代码副本中。您不得在任何源代码版本上提供或强加任何条款，以更改或限制本许可证的适用版本或接受者在本许可证下的权利。但是，您可以包括一份附加文档，提供第3.5节中所述的附加权利。\n\n3.2.源代码的可用性。根据本许可证的条款，您创建或贡献的任何修改都必须以源代码的形式在与可执行版本相同的媒体上或通过接受的电子分发机制向您提供可执行版本的任何人提供；如果通过电子分发机制提供，则必须在最初可用日期后至少十二(12)个月内保持可用，或在该特定修改的后续版本向这些接收者提供后至少六(6)个月内保持可用。您有责任确保即使电子分发机制由第三方维护，源代码版本仍可用。\n\n3.3.修改说明。您必须使您提供的所有受覆盖代码都包含记录您为创建所涵盖代码所做的更改以及任何更改的日期的文件。您必须包括一个突出的声明，说明修改直接或间接源自初始开发者提供的原始代码，并在(A)源代码和(B)可执行版本或相关文档中描述所涵盖代码的来源或所有权的任何声明中包含初始开发者的姓名。\n\n3.4.知识产权事务\n\n(A)第三方索赔\n如果贡献者知道需要第三方知识产权下的许可证才能行使该贡献者根据第2.1或2.2节授予的权利，则贡献者必须包括一个标题为“Legal”的源代码分发的文本文件，该文件详细描述了索赔和提出索赔的一方，以便收件人知道联系谁。如果贡献者在第3.2节所述的修改可用后获得此类知识，则贡献者应立即修改贡献者此后提供的所有副本中的法律文件，并应采取合理的其他步骤(例如通知适当的邮件列表或新闻组)，以通知收到所涵盖代码的人已获得新的知识。\n\n(B)贡献者API\n如果贡献者的修改包括应用程序编程接口，并且贡献者知道实施该API合理所需的专利许可，则贡献者还必须在法律文件中包含此信息。\n\n(C)申述。\n贡献者声明，除根据上述第3.4(A)节披露的情况外，贡献者认为贡献者的修改是贡献者的原创作品(S)和/或贡献者有足够的权利授予本许可证所传达的权利。\n\n3.5.所需的通知。您必须在附件A中复制该通知在源代码的每个文件中。如果由于其结构原因，无法将此类通知放入特定源代码文件中，则您必须在用户可能会查找此类通知的位置(如相关目录)中包含此类通知。如果您创建了一项或多项修改(S)，您可以将您的姓名作为贡献者添加到附件A中描述的通知中。您还必须在描述接受者权利或与所涵盖代码相关的所有权的任何源代码文档中复制本许可证。您可以选择向所涵盖代码的一个或多个收件人提供保修、支持、赔偿或责任义务，并收取费用。但是，您只能代表您自己这样做，而不能代表最初的开发者或任何贡献者。您必须绝对明确，任何此类保证、支持、赔偿或责任义务都是由您单独提供的，并且您在此同意赔偿初始开发者和每个贡献者因您提供的保证、支持、赔偿或责任条款而产生的任何责任。\n\n3.6.可执行版本的分发。仅当所涵盖代码满足第3.1、3.2、3.3、3.4和3.5节的要求，并且您在声明中声明所涵盖代码的源代码版本根据本许可证的条款可用时，您才能以可执行形式分发所涵盖代码，包括对您如何以及在何处履行第3.2节义务的描述。该通知必须显眼地包含在任何可执行版本的通知、相关文件或宣传品中，而您在该通知中描述了收件人对所涵盖代码的相关权利。您可以根据您选择的许可证分发所涵盖代码或所有权的可执行版本，该许可证可能包含与本许可证不同的条款，前提是您遵守本许可证的条款，并且可执行版本的许可证不会试图限制或更改接受者在源代码版本中的权利，而不是本许可证中规定的权利。如果您在不同的许可证下分发可执行版本，您必须绝对明确，任何与本许可证不同的条款都是由您单独提供的，而不是由初始开发者或任何贡献者提供。您在此同意赔偿初始开发者和每个贡献者因您提供的任何此类条款而产生的任何责任。\n\n3.7.更大的作品。您可以通过将所涵盖的代码与不受本许可证条款管辖的其他代码相结合来创建较大的作品，并将较大的作品作为单个产品分发。在这种情况下，您必须确保所涵盖代码满足本许可证的要求。\n\n4.因法规或规章而不能遵守的。\n\n如果由于法规、司法命令或法规的原因，您无法就所涵盖的部分或全部代码遵守本许可证的任何条款，则您必须：(A)最大限度地遵守本许可证的条款；以及(B)描述限制及其影响的代码。此类描述必须包含在3.4节中描述的法律文件中，并且必须包含在源代码的所有分发版本中。除法规或条例禁止的范围外，此类描述必须足够详细，使普通技术人员能够理解。\n\n5.本许可证的适用范围。\n本许可证适用于初始开发者附加了附件A中的通知的代码以及相关的涵盖代码。\n\n6.许可证的版本。\n\n6.1.新版本\nNetscape Communications Corporation(“Netscape”)可能会不时发布本许可证的修订版本和/或新版本。每个版本都会有一个不同的版本号。\n\n6.2.新版本的效果\nONCE所涵盖的代码已在特定版本的许可证下发布，您可以始终根据该版本的条款继续使用它。您也可以选择根据Netscape发布的许可证的任何后续版本的条款使用此类所涵盖的代码。除Netscape外，其他任何人均无权修改适用于根据本许可证创建的所涵盖代码的条款。\n\n6.3.衍生作品\n如果您创建或使用本许可证的修改版本(您这样做可能只是为了将其应用于不受本许可证管辖的代码)，您必须(A)重命名您的许可证，以使“Mozilla”、“MOZILLAPL”、“MOZPL”、“Netscape”、“MPL”、“NPL”或任何令人困惑的相似短语不会出现在您的许可证中(除非注意，您的许可证与本许可证不同)，并且(B)以其他方式明确您的许可证版本包含不同于Mozilla公共许可证和Netscape公共许可证的条款。(在附件A中描述的通知中填写初始开发者、原始代码或贡献者的名称本身不应被视为对本许可证的修改。)\n\n7.免责声明\n根据本许可证，所涵盖的代码是按原样提供的，不提供任何明示或默示的担保，包括但不限于对所涵盖的代码没有缺陷、可销售、适合特定用途或不侵权的担保。有关所涵盖代码的质量和性能的全部风险由您承担。如果任何所涵盖的代码被证明在任何方面有缺陷，您(不是最初的开发者或任何其他贡献者)承担任何必要的服务、修复或更正的费用。本免责声明是本许可证的重要组成部分。除本免责声明外，不得在本协议下授权使用任何所涵盖的代码。\n\n8.终止合同\n\n8.1.如果您不遵守本许可证和根据本许可证授予的权利，本许可证将自动终止并未在知悉违规行为后30天内纠正此类违规行为。适当授予的对所涵盖代码的所有从属许可在本许可证的任何终止后仍然有效。根据其性质，在本许可证终止后必须保持有效的条款将继续有效。\n\n8.2.如果您通过对初始开发者或贡献者(您提起诉讼的初始开发者或贡献者称为“参与者”)主张专利侵权索赔(不包括解密判决诉讼)来发起诉讼：\n\n答：该参与者的贡献人版本直接或间接侵犯了任何专利，则该参与者根据本许可证第2.1和/或2.2节向您授予的任何和所有权利应在参与者发出60天通知后预期终止，除非您在收到通知后60天内：(I)书面同意就您过去和将来使用该参与者所做的修改向参与者支付双方同意的合理版税，或(Ii)撤回您针对该参与者的贡献人版本的诉讼索赔。如果在通知的60天内，双方未以书面形式就合理的特许权使用费和付款安排达成一致，或诉讼索赔未被撤回，则参与者根据第2.1条和/或2.2条授予您的权利将在上述60天通知期限届满时自动终止。\nB.除该参与者的贡献者版本以外的任何软件、硬件或设备直接或间接侵犯任何专利，则该参与者根据第2.1(B)条和第2.2(B)条授予您的任何权利自您首次对该参与者所做的修改进行、使用、销售、分发或进行修改之日起生效。\n\n8.3.如果您对参与者提出专利侵权索赔，声称该参与者的贡献者VersioN直接或间接侵犯任何专利如果在发起专利侵权诉讼之前，此类索赔已得到解决(例如通过许可或和解)，则在确定任何付款或许可的金额或价值时，应考虑该参与者根据第2.1或2.2条授予的许可的合理价值。\n\n8.4.如果根据上述条款8.1或8.2终止，您或任何分销商在终止前在本协议项下有效授予的所有最终用户许可协议(不包括分销商和经销商)在终止后仍然有效。\n\n9.法律责任的限制\n在任何情况下，根据任何法律理论，无论侵权(包括疏忽)、合同或其他，您、初始开发者、任何其他贡献者、所涵盖代码的任何分发者或任何此等各方的任何供应商，都不对任何人承担任何间接、特殊、附带或后果性的损害，包括但不限于商誉损失、停工、计算机故障或故障的损害，或任何和所有其他商业损害或损失，即使此方已被告知此类损害的可能性。在适用法律禁止的范围内，这一责任限制不适用于该当事人的疏忽造成的死亡或人身伤害的责任。某些司法管辖区不允许排除或限制附带或后果性损害，因此此排除和限制可能不适用于您。\n\n10.美国政府终端用户\n按照48C.F.R.2.101(1995年10月)中对该术语的定义，所涵盖的代码是“商业项目”，包括“商业计算机软件”和“商业计算机软件文档”，如第48 C.F.R.12.212(2015年9月)中所使用的术语。1995年)。与48 C.F.R.227.7202-1至227.7202-4(1995年6月)的48 C.F.R.12.212和48 C.F.R.12.212一致，所有美国政府最终用户获得的承保代码仅在此规定的软管权利。\n\n11.杂项\n本许可证代表与本协议主题相关的完整协议。如果本许可证的任何条款被认为是不可执行的，应仅在使其可执行所需的范围内对该条款进行改革。本许可证应受加利福尼亚州法律条款的管辖(除非适用法律另有规定)，不包括其法律冲突条款。对于至少一方是美国公民或被特许或注册在美利坚合众国开展业务的实体的纠纷，任何与本许可证有关的诉讼应受加利福尼亚州北区联邦法院的管辖，诉讼地点位于加利福尼亚州圣克拉拉县，败诉方负责费用，包括但不限于法院费用和合理的律师费和开支。《联合国国际货物销售合同公约》的适用被明确排除在外。任何规定合同语言应被解释为对起草人不利的法律或法规不适用于本许可证。\n\n12.索赔责任\n在初始开发者和贡献者之间，每一方都对因使用本许可证下的权利而直接或间接产生的索赔和损害负责，您同意与初始开发者和贡献者合作，在公平的基础上分配此类责任。本协议没有任何意图，也不应被视为构成任何责任的承认。\n\n13.多许可代码\n初始开发者可将所涵盖代码的某些部分指定为“多重许可”。“多重许可”是指初始开发者允许您在您选择的MPL或初始开发者在附件A中描述的文件中指定的替代许可证(如果有)下使用所涵盖代码的一部分。\n\n附件A-Mozilla公共许可证。\n\n“此文件的内容受Mozilla公共许可证版本1.1(”许可证“)的约束；除非符合许可证，否则您不能使用此文件。您可以在http://www.mozilla.org/MPL/获取许可证的副本\n\n根据本许可证分发的软件是按原样分发的，不提供任何明示或默示的担保。有关许可证下管理权利和限制的特定语言，请参阅许可证。\n\n原始代码为_。\n\n原始代码的初始开发者为_。\n由_创建的部分版权所有(C)_\n_______________________。版权所有。\n\n撰稿人(S)：_。\n\n或者，本文件的内容可根据_许可证(“[_]许可证”)的条款使用，在这种情况下，适用[_]许可证的规定，而不适用上述条款。如果您希望仅在[_]许可证的条款下允许使用您的此文件版本，而不允许其他人在MPL下使用您的此文件版本，请删除上述条款，并以[_]许可证所需的通知和其他条款取而代之，以表明您的决定。如果您不删除上述条款，则收件人可以在MPL或[_]许可证下使用您版本的本文件。\n\n注：本附件A的文本可能与原始代码源代码文件中的通知文本略有不同。您应该使用本附件A的文本进行修改，而不是使用原始代码源代码中的文本。', 'This license has been superseded by v2.0');
INSERT INTO `license` VALUES (240, '2023-05-11 23:28:24', 'BSD-3-Clause-Open-MPI', 'BSD 3-Clause Open MPI variant', 'https://www.open-mpi.org/community/license.php,http://www.netlib.org/lapack/LICENSE.txt', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 'Redistribution and use in source and binary forms, with or without modification, are permitted provided that the following conditions are met:\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"-\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Redistributions of source code must retain the above copyright notice, this list of conditions and the following disclaimer.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"-\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Redistributions in binary form must reproduce the above copyright notice, this list of conditions and the following disclaimer listed in this license in the documentation and/or other materials provided with the distribution.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"-\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Neither the name of the copyright holders nor the names of its contributors may be used to endorse or promote products derived from this software without specific prior written permission.\n\nThe copyright holders provide no reassurances that the source code provided does not infringe any patent, copyright, or any other intellectual property rights of third parties. The copyright holders disclaim any liability to any recipient for claims brought against recipient by any third party for infringement of that parties intellectual property rights.\n\nTHIS SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED BY THE COPYRIGHT HOLDERS AND CONTRIBUTORS \"AS IS\" AND ANY EXPRESS OR IMPLIED WARRANTIES, INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, THE IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY AND FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE ARE DISCLAIMED. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE COPYRIGHT OWNER OR CONTRIBUTORS BE LIABLE FOR ANY DIRECT, INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, EXEMPLARY, OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES (INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, PROCUREMENT OF SUBSTITUTE GOODS OR SERVICES; LOSS OF USE, DATA, OR PROFITS; OR BUSINESS INTERRUPTION) HOWEVER CAUSED AND ON ANY THEORY OF LIABILITY, WHETHER IN CONTRACT, STRICT LIABILITY, OR TORT (INCLUDING NEGLIGENCE OR OTHERWISE) ARISING IN ANY WAY OUT OF THE USE OF THIS SOFTWARE, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGE.', 'Redistribution and use in source and binary forms, with or without\nmodification, are permitted provided that the following conditions are\nmet:\n\n- Redistributions of source code must retain the above copyright\n  notice, this list of conditions and the following disclaimer.\n\n- Redistributions in binary form must reproduce the above copyright\n  notice, this list of conditions and the following disclaimer listed\n  in this license in the documentation and/or other materials\n  provided with the distribution.\n\n- Neither the name of the copyright holders nor the names of its\n  contributors may be used to endorse or promote products derived from\n  this software without specific prior written permission.\n\nThe copyright holders provide no reassurances that the source code\nprovided does not infringe any patent, copyright, or any other\nintellectual property rights of third parties.  The copyright holders\ndisclaim any liability to any recipient for claims brought against\nrecipient by any third party for infringement of that parties\nintellectual property rights.\n\nTHIS SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED BY THE COPYRIGHT HOLDERS AND CONTRIBUTORS\n\"AS IS\" AND ANY EXPRESS OR IMPLIED WARRANTIES, INCLUDING, BUT NOT\nLIMITED TO, THE IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY AND FITNESS FOR\nA PARTICULAR PURPOSE ARE DISCLAIMED. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE COPYRIGHT\nOWNER OR CONTRIBUTORS BE LIABLE FOR ANY DIRECT, INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL,\nSPECIAL, EXEMPLARY, OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES (INCLUDING, BUT NOT\nLIMITED TO, PROCUREMENT OF SUBSTITUTE GOODS OR SERVICES; LOSS OF USE,\nDATA, OR PROFITS; OR BUSINESS INTERRUPTION) HOWEVER CAUSED AND ON ANY\nTHEORY OF LIABILITY, WHETHER IN CONTRACT, STRICT LIABILITY, OR TORT\n(INCLUDING NEGLIGENCE OR OTHERWISE) ARISING IN ANY WAY OUT OF THE USE\nOF THIS SOFTWARE, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGE.', '以源代码和二进制形式重新分发和使用，带或不带\n在满足以下条件的情况下，允许修改\nMET：\n\n-源代码的再分发必须保留上述版权\n请注意，此条件列表和以下免责声明。\n\n-二进制形式的再分发必须复制上述版权\n请注意，此条件列表和下列免责声明\n在本许可证的文档和/或其他材料中\n随发行版一起提供。\n\n-既不是版权所有者的名称，也不是其\n投稿人可能被用来代言或推广源自\n本软件未经明确的事先书面许可。\n\n版权所有者不能保证源代码\n只要不侵犯任何专利、版权或任何其他\n第三方的知识产权。版权持有者\n对任何收件人提出的索赔，不承担任何责任\n任何第三方因侵权行为而收受\n知识产权。\n\n本软件由版权所有者和贡献者提供\n以及任何明示或默示的保证，包括但不包括\n仅限于对适销性和适宜性的默示保证\n一个特定的目的被放弃。在任何情况下，版权不得\n所有者或贡献者对任何直接、间接、附带、\n特殊、惩罚性或后果性损害(包括但不包括\n仅限于代用品或服务的采购；失去使用；\n数据、利润或业务中断)\n责任理论，无论是合同责任、严格责任还是侵权责任\n(包括疏忽或其他)因使用而以任何方式产生的\n即使被告知可能会受到此类损坏，也不会对本软件造成任何影响。', 'This license is largely similar to BSD-3-Clause, but notably includes an additional paragraph between the three main clauses and the all-caps disclaimer text.');
INSERT INTO `license` VALUES (241, '2023-05-11 23:28:24', 'CERN-OHL-1.2', 'CERN Open Hardware Licence v1.2', 'https://www.ohwr.org/project/licenses/wikis/cern-ohl-v1.2', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, '<<beginOptional>> CERN OHL v1.2\n\n2013-09-06 - CERN, Geneva, Switzerland\n\nCERN Open Hardware Licence v1.2<<endOptional>>\n\nPreamble\n\nThrough this CERN Open Hardware Licence (\"CERN OHL\") version 1.2, CERN wishes to provide a tool to foster collaboration and sharing among hardware designers. The CERN OHL is copyright CERN. Anyone is welcome to use the CERN OHL, in unmodified form only, for the distribution of their own Open Hardware designs. Any other right is reserved. Release of hardware designs under the CERN OHL does not constitute an endorsement of the licensor or its designs nor does it imply any involvement by CERN in the development of such designs.\n\n1. Definitions\n\nIn this Licence, the following terms have the following meanings:\n\n\"Licence\" means this CERN OHL.\n\n\"Documentation\" means schematic diagrams, designs, circuit or circuit board layouts, mechanical drawings, flow charts and descriptive text, and other explanatory material that is explicitly stated as being made available under the conditions of this Licence. The Documentation may be in any medium, including but not limited to computer files and representations on paper, film, or any other media.\n\n\"Documentation Location\" means a location where the Licensor has placed Documentation, and which he believes will be publicly accessible for at least three years from the first communication to the public or distribution of Documentation.\n\n\"Product\" means either an entire, or any part of a, device built using the Documentation or the modified Documentation.\n\n\"Licensee\" means any natural or legal person exercising rights under this Licence.\n\n\"Licensor\" means any natural or legal person that creates or modifies Documentation and subsequently communicates to the public and/ or distributes the resulting Documentation under the terms and conditions of this Licence.\n\nA Licensee may at the same time be a Licensor, and vice versa.\n\nUse of the masculine gender includes the feminine and neuter genders and is employed solely to facilitate reading.\n\n\n\n2. Applicability\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"2.1.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> This Licence governs the use, copying, modification, communication to the public and distribution of the Documentation, and the manufacture and distribution of Products. By exercising any right granted under this Licence, the Licensee irrevocably accepts these terms and conditions.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"2.2.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> This Licence is granted by the Licensor directly to the Licensee, and shall apply worldwide and without limitation in time. The Licensee may assign his licence rights or grant sub-licences.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"2.3.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> This Licence does not extend to software, firmware, or code loaded into programmable devices which may be used in conjunction with the Documentation, the modified Documentation or with Products, unless such software, firmware, or code is explicitly expressed to be subject to this Licence. The use of such software, firmware, or code is otherwise subject to the applicable licence terms and conditions.\n\n3. Copying, modification, communication to the public and distribution of the Documentation\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"3.1.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> The Licensee shall keep intact all copyright and trademarks notices, all notices referring to Documentation Location, and all notices that refer to this Licence and to the disclaimer of warranties that are included in the Documentation. He shall include a copy thereof in every copy of the Documentation or, as the case may be, modified Documentation, that he communicates to the public or distributes.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"3.2.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> The Licensee may copy, communicate to the public and distribute verbatim copies of the Documentation, in any medium, subject to the requirements specified in section 3.1.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"3.3.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> The Licensee may modify the Documentation or any portion thereof provided that upon modification of the Documentation, the Licensee shall make the modified Documentation available from a Documentation Location such that it can be easily located by an original Licensor once the Licensee communicates to the public or distributes the modified Documentation under section 3.4, and, where required by section 4.1, by a recipient of a Product. However, the Licensor shall not assert his rights under the foregoing proviso unless or until a Product is distributed.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"3.4.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> The Licensee may communicate to the public and distribute the modified Documentation (thereby in addition to being a Licensee also becoming a Licensor), always provided that he shall:\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"a)\";match=\".{0,20}\">> comply with section 3.1;\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"b)\";match=\".{0,20}\">> cause the modified Documentation to carry prominent notices stating that the Licensee has modified the Documentation, with the date and description of the modifications;\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"c)\";match=\".{0,20}\">> cause the modified Documentation to carry a new Documentation Location notice if the original Documentation provided for one;\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"d)\";match=\".{0,20}\">> make available the modified Documentation at the same level of abstraction as that of the Documentation, in the preferred format for making modifications to it (e.g. the native format of the CAD tool as applicable), and in the event that format is proprietary, in a format viewable with a tool licensed under an OSI-approved license if the proprietary tool can create it; and\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"e)\";match=\".{0,20}\">> license the modified Documentation under the terms and conditions of this Licence or, where applicable, a later version of this Licence as may be issued by CERN.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"3.5.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> The Licence includes a non-exclusive licence to those patents or registered designs that are held by, under the control of, or sub-licensable by the Licensor, to the extent necessary to make use of the rights granted under this Licence. The scope of this section 3.5 shall be strictly limited to the parts of the Documentation or modified Documentation created by the Licensor.\n\n4. Manufacture and distribution of Products\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"4.1.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> The Licensee may manufacture or distribute Products always provided that, where such manufacture or distribution requires a licence under this Licence the Licensee provides to each recipient of such Products an easy means of accessing a copy of the Documentation or modified Documentation, as applicable, as set out in section 3.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"4.2.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> The Licensee is invited to inform any Licensor who has indicated his wish to receive this information about the type, quantity and dates of production of Products the Licensee has (had) manufactured\n\n5. Warranty and liability\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"5.1.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> DISCLAIMER – The Documentation and any modified Documentation are provided \"as is\" and any express or implied warranties, including, but not limited to, implied warranties of merchantability, of satisfactory quality, non-infringement of third party rights, and fitness for a particular purpose or use are disclaimed in respect of the Documentation, the modified Documentation or any Product. The Licensor makes no representation that the Documentation, modified Documentation, or any Product, does or will not infringe any patent, copyright, trade secret or other proprietary right. The entire risk as to the use, quality, and performance of a Product shall be with the Licensee and not the Licensor. This disclaimer of warranty is an essential part of this Licence and a condition for the grant of any rights granted under this Licence. The Licensee warrants that it does not act in a consumer capacity.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"5.2.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> LIMITATION OF LIABILITY – The Licensor shall have no liability for direct, indirect, special, incidental, consequential, exemplary, punitive or other damages of any character including, without limitation, procurement of substitute goods or services, loss of use, data or profits, or business interruption, however caused and on any theory of contract, warranty, tort (including negligence), product liability or otherwise, arising in any way in relation to the Documentation, modified Documentation and/or the use, manufacture or distribution of a Product, even if advised of the possibility of such damages, and the Licensee shall hold the Licensor(s) free and harmless from any liability, costs, damages, fees and expenses, including claims by third parties, in relation to such use.\n\n6. General\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"6.1.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Except for the rights explicitly granted hereunder, this Licence does not imply or represent any transfer or assignment of intellectual property rights to the Licensee.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"6.2.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> The Licensee shall not use or make reference to any of the names (including acronyms and abbreviations), images, or logos under which the Licensor is known, save in so far as required to comply with section 3. Any such permitted use or reference shall be factual and shall in no event suggest any kind of endorsement by the Licensor or its personnel of the modified Documentation or any Product, or any kind of implication by the Licensor or its personnel in the preparation of the modified Documentation or Product.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"6.3.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> CERN may publish updated versions of this Licence which retain the same general provisions as this version, but differ in detail so far this is required and reasonable. New versions will be published with a unique version number.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"6.4.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> This Licence shall terminate with immediate effect, upon written notice and without involvement of a court if the Licensee fails to comply with any of its terms and conditions, or if the Licensee initiates legal action against Licensor in relation to this Licence. Section 5 shall continue to apply.', 'CERN OHL v1.2\n2013-09-06 - CERN, Geneva, Switzerland\nCERN Open Hardware Licence v1.2\n\nPreamble\nThrough this CERN Open Hardware Licence (\"CERN OHL\") version 1.2, CERN wishes to provide a tool to foster collaboration and sharing among hardware designers. The CERN OHL is copyright CERN. Anyone is welcome to use the CERN OHL, in unmodified form only, for the distribution of their own Open Hardware designs. Any other right is reserved. Release of hardware designs under the CERN OHL does not constitute an endorsement of the licensor or its designs nor does it imply any involvement by CERN in the development of such designs.\n\n1. Definitions\nIn this Licence, the following terms have the following meanings:\n“Licence” means this CERN OHL.\n“Documentation” means schematic diagrams, designs, circuit or circuit board layouts, mechanical drawings, flow charts and descriptive text, and other explanatory material that is explicitly stated as being made available under the conditions of this Licence. The Documentation may be in any medium, including but not limited to computer files and representations on paper, film, or any other media.\n“Documentation Location” means a location where the Licensor has placed Documentation, and which he believes will be publicly accessible for at least three years from the first communication to the public or distribution of Documentation.\n“Product” means either an entire, or any part of a, device built using the Documentation or the modified Documentation.\n“Licensee” means any natural or legal person exercising rights under this Licence.\n“Licensor” means any natural or legal person that creates or modifies Documentation and subsequently communicates to the public and/ or distributes the resulting Documentation under the terms and conditions of this Licence.\nA Licensee may at the same time be a Licensor, and vice versa.\nUse of the masculine gender includes the feminine and neuter genders and is employed solely to facilitate reading.\n\n2. Applicability\n2.1. This Licence governs the use, copying, modification, communication to the public and distribution of the Documentation, and the manufacture and distribution of Products. By exercising any right granted under this Licence, the Licensee irrevocably accepts these terms and conditions.\n2.2. This Licence is granted by the Licensor directly to the Licensee, and shall apply worldwide and without limitation in time. The Licensee may assign his licence rights or grant sub-licences.\n2.3. This Licence does not extend to software, firmware, or code loaded into programmable devices which may be used in conjunction with the Documentation, the modified Documentation or with Products, unless such software, firmware, or code is explicitly expressed to be subject to this Licence. The use of such software, firmware, or code is otherwise subject to the applicable licence terms and conditions.\n\n3. Copying, modification, communication to the public and distribution of the Documentation\n3.1. The Licensee shall keep intact all copyright and trademarks notices, all notices referring to Documentation Location, and all notices that refer to this Licence and to the disclaimer of warranties that are included in the Documentation. He shall include a copy thereof in every copy of the Documentation or, as the case may be, modified Documentation, that he communicates to the public or distributes.\n3.2. The Licensee may copy, communicate to the public and distribute verbatim copies of the Documentation, in any medium, subject to the requirements specified in section 3.1.\n3.3. The Licensee may modify the Documentation or any portion thereof provided that upon modification of the Documentation, the Licensee shall make the modified Documentation available from a Documentation Location such that it can be easily located by an original Licensor once the Licensee communicates to the public or distributes the modified Documentation under section 3.4, and, where required by section 4.1, by a recipient of a Product. However, the Licensor shall not assert his rights under the foregoing proviso unless or until a Product is distributed.\n3.4. The Licensee may communicate to the public and distribute the modified Documentation (thereby in addition to being a Licensee also becoming a Licensor), always provided that he shall:\na) comply with section 3.1;\nb) cause the modified Documentation to carry prominent notices stating that the Licensee has modified the Documentation, with the date and description of the modifications;\nc) cause the modified Documentation to carry a new Documentation Location notice if the original Documentation provided for one;\nd) make available the modified Documentation at the same level of abstraction as that of the Documentation, in the preferred format for making modifications to it (e.g. the native format of the CAD tool as applicable), and in the event that format is proprietary, in a format viewable with a tool licensed under an OSI-approved license if the proprietary tool can create it; and\ne) license the modified Documentation under the terms and conditions of this Licence or, where applicable, a later version of this Licence as may be issued by CERN.\n3.5. The Licence includes a non-exclusive licence to those patents or registered designs that are held by, under the control of, or sub-licensable by the Licensor, to the extent necessary to make use of the rights granted under this Licence. The scope of this section 3.5 shall be strictly limited to the parts of the Documentation or modified Documentation created by the Licensor.\n\n4. Manufacture and distribution of Products\n4.1. The Licensee may manufacture or distribute Products always provided that, where such manufacture or distribution requires a licence under this Licence the Licensee provides to each recipient of such Products an easy means of accessing a copy of the Documentation or modified Documentation, as applicable, as set out in section 3.\n4.2. The Licensee is invited to inform any Licensor who has indicated his wish to receive this information about the type, quantity and dates of production of Products the Licensee has (had) manufactured\n\n5. Warranty and liability\n5.1. DISCLAIMER – The Documentation and any modified Documentation are provided \"as is\" and any express or implied warranties, including, but not limited to, implied warranties of merchantability, of satisfactory quality, non-infringement of third party rights, and fitness for a particular purpose or use are disclaimed in respect of the Documentation, the modified Documentation or any Product. The Licensor makes no representation that the Documentation, modified Documentation, or any Product, does or will not infringe any patent, copyright, trade secret or other proprietary right. The entire risk as to the use, quality, and performance of a Product shall be with the Licensee and not the Licensor. This disclaimer of warranty is an essential part of this Licence and a condition for the grant of any rights granted under this Licence. The Licensee warrants that it does not act in a consumer capacity.\n5.2. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY – The Licensor shall have no liability for direct, indirect, special, incidental, consequential, exemplary, punitive or other damages of any character including, without limitation, procurement of substitute goods or services, loss of use, data or profits, or business interruption, however caused and on any theory of contract, warranty, tort (including negligence), product liability or otherwise, arising in any way in relation to the Documentation, modified Documentation and/or the use, manufacture or distribution of a Product, even if advised of the possibility of such damages, and the Licensee shall hold the Licensor(s) free and harmless from any liability, costs, damages, fees and expenses, including claims by third parties, in relation to such use.\n\n6. General\n6.1. Except for the rights explicitly granted hereunder, this Licence does not imply or represent any transfer or assignment of intellectual property rights to the Licensee.\n6.2. The Licensee shall not use or make reference to any of the names (including acronyms and abbreviations), images, or logos under which the Licensor is known, save in so far as required to comply with section 3. Any such permitted use or reference shall be factual and shall in no event suggest any kind of endorsement by the Licensor or its personnel of the modified Documentation or any Product, or any kind of implication by the Licensor or its personnel in the preparation of the modified Documentation or Product.\n6.3. CERN may publish updated versions of this Licence which retain the same general provisions as this version, but differ in detail so far this is required and reasonable. New versions will be published with a unique version number.\n6.4. This Licence shall terminate with immediate effect, upon written notice and without involvement of a court if the Licensee fails to comply with any of its terms and conditions, or if the Licensee initiates legal action against Licensor in relation to this Licence. Section 5 shall continue to apply.', 'CERN OHL v1.2\n2013-09-06-欧洲核子研究中心，瑞士日内瓦\nCERN开放硬件许可证v1.2\n\n前言\n通过CERN开放硬件许可证(“CERN OHL”)1.2版，CERN希望提供一种工具来促进硬件设计者之间的合作和共享。CERN OHL版权所有。欢迎任何人使用CERN OHL，仅限于未经修改的形式，用于分发他们自己的开放式硬件设计。任何其他权利均保留。根据CERN OHL发布硬件设计并不构成对许可方或其设计的认可，也不意味着CERN参与此类设计的开发。\n\n1.定义\n在本许可证中，下列术语具有以下含义：\n“许可证”指本CERN OHL。\n“文件”系指原理图、设计、电路板或电路板布局、机械图纸、流程图和说明性文本，以及根据本许可证条件明确声明的其他说明性材料。文件可以是任何媒体，包括但不限于计算机文件和纸、胶片或任何其他媒体上的表示。\n“文件位置”是指许可方放置文件的位置，他认为自文件首次向公众传达或分发起，该位置至少三年内可向公众开放。\n“产品”是指使用文档或修改后的文档构建的整个设备或设备的任何部分。\n“被许可人”是指在本许可证项下行使权利的任何自然人或法人。\n“许可方”是指根据本许可证的条款和条件创建或修改文档并随后向公众传达和/或分发生成的文档的任何自然人或法人。\n被许可方可以同时是许可方，反之亦然。\n男性的用法包括女性和中性性别，仅用于方便阅读。\n\n2.适用性\n2.1.本许可证管理文件的使用、复制、修改、向公众传播和分发，以及产品的制造和分发。通过行使根据本许可证授予的任何权利，被许可方不可撤销地接受这些条款和条件。\n2.2.本许可证由许可方直接授予被许可方，应在全球范围内且不受时间限制地适用。被许可人可以转让其许可权或授予转授许可。\n2.3.本许可证不适用于加载到可编程设备中的软件、固件或代码，这些软件、固件或代码可与文档、修改后的文档或产品一起使用，除非该软件、固件或代码明确表示受本许可证的约束。此类软件、固件或代码的使用受适用的许可条款和条件的约束。\n\n3.文件的复制、修改、向公众传播和分发\n3.1.被许可方应保持文档中包含的所有版权和商标声明、与文档位置有关的所有声明以及与本许可证和担保免责声明相关的所有声明保持不变。他应在他向公众传达或分发的每份文件或经修改的文件(视属何情况而定)中包括该文件的副本。\n3.2.被许可人可按照第3.1节规定的要求，在任何媒介上复制、向公众传达和分发文件的逐字副本。\n3.3.被许可方可以修改文件或其任何部分，但条件是在修改文件时，被许可方应使修改后的文件在文件位置可用，以便一旦被许可方根据第3.4条向公众传达或分发修改后的文件，原始许可方即可轻松找到修改后的文件，并在4.1条要求的情况下，由接收方找到修改后的文件F a产品。但是，在产品分发之前，许可方不得主张其在前述但书下的权利。\n3.4.被许可方可以向公众传达和分发修改后的文件(从而除了成为被许可方外，还可以成为许可方)，条件是他应：\nA)遵守第3.1节；\nB)使修改后的文件带有显眼的通知，说明被许可人已修改文件，并注明修改的日期和说明；\nC)如果原始文件提供了新的文件位置通知，则使修改后的文件带有新的文件位置通知；\nD)使修改后的文件与文件的抽象程度相同，以对其进行修改的首选格式(例如，适用的CAD工具的本地格式)提供，如果该格式是专有的，则以在OSI批准的许可证下许可的工具可查看的格式提供，如果专有工具可以创建该文件；以及\nE)根据本许可证的条款和条件，或在适用的情况下，根据CERN可能发布的本许可证的较新版本，对修改后的文档进行许可。\n3.5.本许可证包括对许可方持有、在许可方控制下或可由许可方再许可的专利或注册外观设计的非排他性许可，在使用根据本许可授予的权利所必需的范围内。第3.5节的范围应严格限于许可方创建的文档或修改后的文档的部分。\n\n4.产品的制造和分销\n4.1.被许可方可以制造或分销产品，但前提是，如果此类制造或分销需要本许可证项下的许可证，则被许可方应向此类产品的每个接受者提供一种方便的方式，以获取第3节所列的文件副本或经修改的文件(如适用)。\n4.2.请被许可方告知Y许可方表示希望收到有关被许可方生产的产品的类型、数量和生产日期的信息\n\n5.保证及法律责任\n5.1.免责声明-文档和任何修改后的文档按原样提供，对于文档、修改后的文档或任何产品，拒绝提供任何明示或默示的保证，包括但不限于对适销性、质量令人满意、不侵犯第三方权利以及是否适合特定目的或使用的默示保证。许可方不表示文档、修改后的文档或任何产品侵犯或不会侵犯任何专利、版权、商业秘密或其他专有权。产品的使用、质量和性能的全部风险应由被许可方承担，而不是许可方。本免责声明是本许可证的重要组成部分，也是授予根据本许可证授予的任何权利的条件。被许可方保证不以消费者身份行事。\n5.2.责任限制-对于直接、间接、特殊、附带、后果性、惩罚性或其他任何性质的损害，包括但不限于替代商品或服务的采购、使用损失、数据或利润或业务中断，许可方不承担任何责任，无论这些损害是由何种原因引起的，并基于任何合同、保修、侵权(包括疏忽)、产品责任或其他理论，以任何方式与文件、修改的文件和/或产品的使用、制造或分销有关，即使被告知此类损害的可能性，许可方也不承担责任。被许可方(S)应免除且不受任何责任、成本、损害与此类使用有关的费用和开支，包括第三方的索赔。\n\n6.一般规定\n6.1.除根据本许可证明确授予的权利外，本许可证不暗示或代表不得将知识产权转让或转让给被许可方。\n6.2.被许可方不得使用或提及许可方为人所知的任何名称(包括缩略语和缩略语)、图像或徽标，除非符合第3条的要求。任何此类允许的使用或提及均应是事实，且在任何情况下不得暗示许可方或其人员对修改的文档或任何产品进行任何形式的认可，或许可方或其人员在修改的文档或产品的准备过程中的任何形式的含意。\n6.3.欧洲核子研究中心可能会发布本许可证的更新版本，其中保留了与本版本相同的一般条款，但在细节上有所不同，因为这是必要的和合理的。新版本将以唯一的版本号发布。\n6.4.如果被许可方未能遵守其任何条款和条件，或者如果被许可方就本许可对许可方提起法律诉讼，则本许可应在书面通知后立即终止，且无需法院介入。第5条继续适用。', NULL);
